{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780635187,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1431ec6001muYlV50i7YdaHj","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e1430859001WMWUMqxrE3PPRq","type":"tool","id":"call_bd7429c9ef9a4ccdaec26c5d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-294\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - vibe-hooks-doctor-5 lineage\n3: description: Runtime strategy tracking review progress for the vibe-hooks-doctor fan-out lineage, fifth pass of command surfacing.\n4: version: 1.11.14.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Review Strategy - vibe-hooks-doctor-5 lineage\n8: \n9: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n10: \n11: ### Purpose\n12: \n13: Persistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n14: (P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\n15: iteration before any review action.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. TOPIC\n20: \n21: Review pass five of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n22: in the `vibe-hooks-doctor` area. Scope: the changed paths listed in\n23: `review/review-scope-5.txt` whose area is `vibe-hooks-doctor` — the doctor command routes, the\n24: hook-wiring check and its tests plus README, the command-reference validator, the Claude\n25: prompt-submit hook, the Vibe prompt advisor, the hook contract doc, the CI workflow, and the\n26: hook test files — plus shared docs that describe them.\n27: \n28: The operator focus is the pass-five brief: the kill switch and direct-call switch paths; command\n29: offers surviving a refusal, question, history statement or bare mention; Vibe journal scoring;\n30: the doctor hooks-file reading; docs against code; and holdout hygiene.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n35: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n36: [All dimensions complete]\n37: \n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n43: \n44: - The kill-switch CLI files (launcher, cli, disabled lib) are the `kill-switch-cli-5` lineage's\n45:   scope. This lineage reads them only as context for the hook paths it owns.\n46: - The transcript scorer and behaviour-arena scripts are the `accuracy-runner-5` lineage's scope.\n47:   This lineage records the boundary and raises findings only where a hook or doctor file is the\n48:   producer.\n49: - The feature-catalog, changelog, playbook and graph-metadata docs are `docs-metadata-5`'s scope;\n50:   they are read here only to check whether a doc describes this area's code falsely.\n51: - Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n52:   `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n53: - No code changes: review is observation-only.\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n58: \n59: - Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\n60: - Cap: `maxIterations` 4.\n61: - Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n62: - Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n67: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n68: - [x] correctness\n69: - [x] security\n70: - [x] traceability\n71: - [x] maintainability\n72: \n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n78: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n79: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n80: - P1 (Required): 0\n81: - P2 (Suggestions): 8\n82: - Resolved: 0\n83: \n84: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n89: \n90: - Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the directive-only context the sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` explicitly supports: `Directives:` at the start makes `indexOf('\\nDirectives:')` miss, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command, while the same probe of the current headed fallback was unchanged (iteration 1).\n91: - Reading `reduceRepeatedHead` first: its explicit `context.startsWith(label)` branch proves the authors know the fallback exists, which isolated the missing guard in `withCommandDocuments` rather than blaming the handler (iteration 1).\n92: - Walking the generated bridge table read-only: 69 of 69 `commandPolicies` rows resolve to a document, so the document-line mechanism is sound and the finding is the fallback boundary, not the resolution rule (iteration 1).\n93: \n94: ---\n95: \n96: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n97: \n98: - Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\n99: - Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).\n100: - Resolving the handler's `new URL('../../../../../../hooks/...', import.meta.url)` with node for both the source and the dist location: the source path lands one level above the repository while the dist path lands on `.skilled/hooks/shared`, which proves the canonical switch gap is source-only and keeps the finding at P2 (iteration 2).\n101: - Following the switch table row by row into the shared resolver and the plugin: both `_HOOK_DISABLED` and `_PLUGIN_DISABLED` sit in one alias list, and the plugin asks the same resolver, so the table's hook-versus-plugin distinction is not in the code (iteration 2).\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 9B. WHAT FAILED (continued)\n106: \n107: - Reading the source handler's switch check as proving the canonical switch failed: the resolver path is wrong from the source folder and the catch returns enabled. Only the explicit legacy-name check survives a source run (iteration 2).\n108: - Reading phase 029's `AC-009` as evidence for the alias rows failed: it verifies that the listed lines did not change, not that they are true (iteration 2).\n109: - Reading the Vibe reader as covering every field the host acts on failed: it reads only `type` and `command`, so a `match` filter is invisible even though the repository's own hooks file uses `match` values, including `agents_spawn` (iteration 3).\n110: - Reading the hook contract's per-runtime section as complete after the Vibe row failed: the section intro and the \"starting a surfaced command\" table still enumerate the older runtimes only (iteration 3).\n111: - Reading the Vibe part's dependency object as fully injectable failed: `env` reaches only the child-session test while the receipt directory keeps reading the process environment, so a caller that injects only `env` writes to the real temporary folder (iteration 4).\n112: - Reading the doctor contract test as covering the Vibe rows by name failed: the route case is still titled for DSH while the array it walks holds both runtimes (iteration 4).\n113: \n114: ---\n115: \n116: ## 9D. WHAT WORKED (continued)\n117: \n118: - Reading the suite's injected `read`/`write` pair against the module's default pair: the suite is hermetic, which isolates the gap to the documented `env` dependency rather than to the tests (iteration 4).\n119: - Reading `MIRROR_CHECKS` and the two gap walks before judging the test name: the coverage is complete and only the title is stale, so the finding stays a naming gap instead of a coverage claim (iteration 4).\n120: \n121: ---\n122: \n123: ## 9C. WHAT WORKED (continued)\n124: \n125: - Running the wiring check on this checkout before judging it: five `ok` lines and exit 0 prove the real `.vibe/hooks.toml` parses through the line reader, so the finding is the ignored `match` field rather than the reader (iteration 3).\n126: - Counting the three Vibe script names in the workflow and the route instead of trusting the comment: nine and three lines match the contract test's assertions and phase 030's `REQ-005` (iteration 3).\n127: - Scanning the twelve scoped files for corpus names: no hit, which is the holdout-hygiene evidence, kept to names and counts (iteration 3).\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n132: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n133: ### **A commented `[[hooks]]` header starts a block.** Ruled out: the header is stripped of its comment before comparison and the test \"reads a commented hooks header as the start of the next block\" passes. -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n134: - What was tried: **A commented `[[hooks]]` header starts a block.** Ruled out: the header is stripped of its comment before comparison and the test \"reads a commented hooks header as the start of the next block\" passes.\n135: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n136: - Do NOT retry: **A commented `[[hooks]]` header starts a block.** Ruled out: the header is stripped of its comment before comparison and the test \"reads a commented hooks header as the start of the next block\" passes.\n137: \n138: ### **A daemon started by a flagged caller stays disabled.** Ruled out: the launcher's allowlist forwards no switch name and no `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG`, so the daemon answers later callers normally. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n139: - What was tried: **A daemon started by a flagged caller stays disabled.** Ruled out: the launcher's allowlist forwards no switch name and no `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG`, so the daemon answers later callers normally.\n140: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n141: - Do NOT retry: **A daemon started by a flagged caller stays disabled.** Ruled out: the launcher's allowlist forwards no switch name and no `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG`, so the daemon answers later callers normally.\n142: \n143: ### **A later table lends its command to the hooks block before it.** Ruled out: any other header clears the current block, with a test for `[[notes]]`. -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n144: - What was tried: **A later table lends its command to the hooks block before it.** Ruled out: any other header clears the current block, with a test for `[[notes]]`.\n145: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n146: - Do NOT retry: **A later table lends its command to the hooks block before it.** Ruled out: any other header clears the current block, with a test for `[[notes]]`.\n147: \n148: ### **A Vibe-only doctor test is missing from CI.** Ruled out: `run-all.sh` globs every `*.test.cjs`, and the `doctor-scripts` job runs it. -- BLOCKED (iteration 4, 1 attempts)\n149: - What was tried: **A Vibe-only doctor test is missing from CI.** Ruled out: `run-all.sh` globs every `*.test.cjs`, and the `doctor-scripts` job runs it.\n150: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n151: - Do NOT retry: **A Vibe-only doctor test is missing from CI.** Ruled out: `run-all.sh` globs every `*.test.cjs`, and the `doctor-scripts` job runs it.\n152: \n153: ### **The `.vibe` allowlist entry accepts a phantom runtime.** Ruled out: `.vibe/agents` is present with generated profiles. -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n154: - What was tried: **The `.vibe` allowlist entry accepts a phantom runtime.** Ruled out: `.vibe/agents` is present with generated profiles.\n155: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n156: - Do NOT retry: **The `.vibe` allowlist entry accepts a phantom runtime.** Ruled out: `.vibe/agents` is present with generated profiles.\n157: \n158: ### **The `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` explici