{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780834747,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14623b4002KwJcN7MPv6TBeT","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e1461bf40019elT2P74ijZpgc","type":"tool","id":"call_c23f9da1bc3247b29f6cfb26","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"match\\|match =\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/guards-and-hooks.md | head -40","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"95:| `match` | no | An optional selector string; it must not be blank when set (`models.py:87-92`). |\n126:| `system-deep-loop-guard.js` | Blocks a `task` dispatch to a deep-loop subagent whose declared mode disagrees with `mode-registry.json`, or a repeated loop-like dispatch. | hook — Vibe spawns subagents through `agents_spawn`, so the guard matches that tool and reads `tool_input.config_name` | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n130:| `system-dist-freshness-guard.js` | Warns when a session or a risky Bash command is about to trust stale local dist outputs. | hook — `session_start` injects the warning as `additional_context`, and a non-strict `post_tool` entry adds the mid-session `STALE DIST WARNING` to the tool result after a write, edit or matched shell command (phase 015's keyed child run) | `session_start`, `post_tool` |\n131:| `system-skill-advisor.js` | Injects the skill advisor brief into each request's system text and exposes the advisor status tool. | hook — the `pre_agent` turn-start composer routes each main-session prompt through the shared advisor handler under the `vibe` label, so the brief arrives as `additional_context` (phase 015's keyed main-session run recorded `Advisor: no skill matched.`) | `pre_agent` |\n195:`tool_name` is the qualified name, `file_system.bash`, while a `match` selector accepts either that or the short `bash` (`SKILL.md:854-858`). `tool_input` holds the model's arguments, here `command` and `timeout`. `parent_session_id` is `null` in a main session and set inside a subagent.\n207:| `0` | anything else | Failure path: free-form text, broken JSON, a scalar, an array or a schema mismatch. |\n234:| Shell guards must match `re:bash\\|process_start` | A background command goes through `process_start`, which `match = \"bash\"` does not catch (`SKILL.md:859-861`). The fixture's `hooks.toml` uses that selector. |\n244:| `.vibe/plugins/repo-guards/fixtures/wire-format/hooks.toml` | One `[[hooks]]` entry: `name = \"wire-fixture\"`, `type = \"pre_tool\"`, `match = \"re:bash\\|process_start\"`, `strict = true`, and a `command` that runs the script with `WIRE_LOG` set. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"95:| `match` | no | An optional selector string; it must not be blank when set (`models.py:87-92`). |\n126:| `system-deep-loop-guard.js` | Blocks a `task` dispatch to a deep-loop subagent whose declared mode disagrees with `mode-registry.json`, or a repeated loop-like dispatch. | hook — Vibe spawns subagents through `agents_spawn`, so the guard matches that tool and reads `tool_input.config_name` | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n130:| `system-dist-freshness-guard.js` | Warns when a session or a risky Bash command is about to trust stale local dist outputs. | hook — `session_start` injects the warning as `additional_context`, and a non-strict `post_tool` entry adds the mid-session `STALE DIST WARNING` to the tool result after a write, edit or matched shell command (phase 015's keyed child run) | `session_start`, `post_tool` |\n131:| `system-skill-advisor.js` | Injects the skill advisor brief into each request's system text and exposes the advisor status tool. | hook — the `pre_agent` turn-start composer routes each main-session prompt through the shared advisor handler under the `vibe` label, so the brief arrives as `additional_context` (phase 015's keyed main-session run recorded `Advisor: no skill matched.`) | `pre_agent` |\n195:`tool_name` is the qualified name, `file_system.bash`, while a `match` selector accepts either that or the short `bash` (`SKILL.md:854-858`). `tool_input` holds the model's arguments, here `command` and `timeout`. `parent_session_id` is `null` in a main session and set inside a subagent.\n207:| `0` | anything else | Failure path: free-form text, broken JSON, a scalar, an array or a schema mismatch. |\n234:| Shell guards must match `re:bash\\|process_start` | A background command goes through `process_start`, which `match = \"bash\"` does not catch (`SKILL.md:859-861`). The fixture's `hooks.toml` uses that selector. |\n244:| `.vibe/plugins/repo-guards/fixtures/wire-format/hooks.toml` | One `[[hooks]]` entry: `name = \"wire-fixture\"`, `type = \"pre_tool\"`, `match = \"re:bash\\|process_start\"`, `strict = true`, and a `command` that runs the script with `WIRE_LOG` set. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"match\\\\|match =\\\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/guards-and-hooks.md | head -40\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780832692,"end":1794780834747}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780834757,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1462685001guSveKr2gGC0Lb","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e1461bf40019elT2P74ijZpgc","type":"tool","id":"call_aeb5bba88d6e420eb328fbe7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"match\" .vibe/plugins/repo-guards/render-home-hooks.cjs | head; echo ===; grep -rn \"match = \\|hooks.toml\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"===\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:37:The folder ships: `.vibe/config.toml`, `.vibe/hooks.toml`, `.vibe/SYNC.md`, the generated agent, skill and prompt mirrors, and the `plugins/repo-guards/` bundle. The three generators under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/vibe/` own the mirrors. The discovery and home behavior below are read from the installed package and observed during research.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:70:| `.vibe/hooks.toml` | Project hook declarations |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:92:| `hooks.toml` | hand-authored | none | Hook declarations; the guard phase owns it |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:108:`hooks.toml` and `plugins/repo-guards/` are hand-authored and belong to the guard phase, which settles the hook wire format. The runtime-folder phase leaves both out, and the folder accepts them later without a generator change.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"===\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:37:The folder ships: `.vibe/config.toml`, `.vibe/hooks.toml`, `.vibe/SYNC.md`, the generated agent, skill and prompt mirrors, and the `plugins/repo-guards/` bundle. The three generators under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/vibe/` own the mirrors. The discovery and home behavior below are read from the installed package and observed during research.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:70:| `.vibe/hooks.toml` | Project hook declarations |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:92:| `hooks.toml` | hand-authored | none | Hook declarations; the guard phase owns it |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md:108:`hooks.toml` and `plugins/repo-guards/` are hand-authored and belong to the guard phase, which settles the hook wire format. The runtime-folder phase leaves both out, and the folder accepts them later without a generator change.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"match\\\" .vibe/plugins/repo-guards/render-home-hooks.cjs | head; echo ===; grep -rn \\\"match = \\\\|hooks.toml\\\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/runtime-folder-and-sync.md | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780833413,"end":1794780834757}}}}
