{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780904802,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1473b63001yKrWvJZrWzg5c8","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e146eb8e001hZmhMdwgaKmta0","type":"tool","id":"call_049536505cdd4459ba94e9d9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/guards-and-hooks.md","offset":60,"limit":80},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/guards-and-hooks.md, lines 60-139\n60: `HookType` declares seven members (`models.py:20-27`). Three accept `strict` (`models.py:31-35`), and the model validator raises a `strict is only valid for ... hooks` error on any other type (`models.py:94-98`).\n61: \n62: | Type | `strict` | Fires | What it can decide |\n63: |---|---|---|---|\n64: | `pre_tool` | yes | Before a tool call | Refuse the call (`_foreign_hooks.py:14`). The only pre-execution seam a guard can use. |\n65: | `post_tool` | yes | After a tool call | Blank the tool result on a strict failure (`_foreign_hooks.py:15`); no run has shown it. |\n66: | `pre_agent` | yes | Before an agent turn | Block the message before the turn runs (`_foreign_hooks.py:16-17`). |\n67: | `post_agent` | no | After an agent turn | A deny sends a retry message the model answers, capped at three retries per turn; the fourth invocation is force-accepted. `strict` is rejected on a declared hook (`_foreign_hooks.py:18-20`), so the deny is the seam, not a held turn (phase 014 recorded `retry, retry, retry, accept`). |\n68: | `notification` | no | An approval or question opens; the main turn completes or fails | Nothing: it runs in the background and its output is ignored (`_host_hooks.py:6-8`). |\n69: | `session_start` | no | A session opens: `startup`, `resume`, `clear` or `fork` | Add `additional_context` to the session's next user message (`_host_hooks.py:9-12,65-83`). |\n70: | `session_end` | no | A session closes: `exit`, `clear` or `other` | Nothing: it runs in the background and its output is ignored (`_host_hooks.py:13-14`). |\n71: \n72: The last three are host hooks: the app server fires them outside the engine's turn (`models.py:37-42`). The first four are engine hooks, and only the engine hooks can refuse work.\n73: \n74: ### What `strict` Buys\n75: \n76: `strict` declares that a failing hook blocks instead of letting the call through. The validator enforces which types may carry it (`models.py:94-98`), and the harness runner's docstring maps a strict failure to a deny at `pre_tool`, a blanked result at `post_tool` and a blocked message at `pre_agent` (`mistralai_vibe_local_harness/vibe/_foreign_hooks.py:9-20`). `post_agent` rejects `strict`, but its conforming deny is not inert: Vibe returns the reason as a retry message, repeats the turn and force-accepts the fourth invocation. Phase 014's `DENY_MODE=always` fixture recorded `retry, retry, retry, accept`, and `turn_id` stayed the same on all four (`scratch/journal-excerpts/deny-always-hook-outcomes.jsonl`). That retry is the seam the turn-end composer uses (section 4), not a held turn. No run has shown a strict failure at any type; the `pre_tool` deny the wire fixture observed is a conforming deny.\n77: \n78: ### Protocols\n79: \n80: `HookProtocol` declares `vibe`, `claude_code` and `kimi_code` (`models.py:59-63`), so a Claude-format hook script is a candidate porting source. `protocol` is a runtime field on `RuntimeHookDefinition` (`models.py:113`), not a `HookConfig` field (`models.py:71-78`), and the default file loader ignores keys it does not model (`config.py:17-24`). A `protocol = \"claude_code\"` line in `hooks.toml` is therefore not how the protocol is selected; the loader or plugin that registers the hook sets it.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 3. DECLARATION AND LOADING\n85: \n86: ### The File\n87: \n88: A project declares hooks in `.vibe/hooks.toml` at the project root; discovery is root-only, like the rest of `.vibe/` ([runtime-folder-and-sync.md](./runtime-folder-and-sync.md) section 2). The file holds a `[[hooks]]` array (`config.py:17-24`), and each entry carries these fields (`models.py:71-78`):\n89: \n90: | Field | Required | Notes |\n91: |---|---|---|\n92: | `name` | yes | Unique across every loaded file; a duplicate is dropped with an issue (`config.py:105-113`). |\n93: | `type` | yes | One of the seven in section 2. |\n94: | `command` | yes | A non-blank command string, run as a subprocess. |\n95: | `match` | no | An optional selector string; it must not be blank when set (`models.py:87-92`). |\n96: | `timeout` | no | Seconds; defaults to 60.0 (`models.py:65,99-101`). |\n97: | `strict` | no | Defaults to false; only the three types in section 2 accept it. |\n98: | `description` | no | Free text. |\n99: \n100: ### The Trust Gate\n101: \n102: The project file loads only in a trusted folder. `_trusted_workdir` returns `None` when the project source is disabled or the cwd is not in the trust store (`_harness_manager.py:99-106`), and `hook_files` builds `<root>/.vibe/hooks.toml` from the project roots (`_harness_manager.py:137-144`). The roots are the trusted cwd plus every `--add-dir` path (`_harness_manager.py:119-135`), so an add-dir root contributes its own file because the operator named it, even when the cwd is untrusted; `$VIBE_HOME/hooks.toml` loads from the home when the user source is enabled (`_harness_manager.py:142-143`).\n103: \n104: Project hooks sit behind the same trust gate as `.vibe/config.toml` ([runtime-folder-and-sync.md](./runtime-folder-and-sync.md) section 2): the folder holding the file must be trusted. `--trust` from a subdirectory trusts only that subdirectory, so a run that must load the repository's hooks lists the checkout root in its home's `trusted_folders.toml`. An untrusted run loads none of them, and no error says so. The home file is the way around the gate: `$VIBE_HOME/hooks.toml` loads under the user source, which is on by default, with no trust entry. The project file names its scripts through `$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)`, which fails outside the checkout, so the home copy replaces that expression with the resolved root, and the renderer refuses the operator's own `~/.vibe`, where the guards would reach every Vibe session on the machine.\n105: \n106: ### Load Order and Failures\n107: \n108: Hooks run project file, project plugins, user file, then global plugins (`_runtime.py:2752-2753`). A duplicate `name` keeps the first and records an issue for the rest (`config.py:105-113`). A file that fails to parse contributes no hooks and records why (`config.py:56-61,69-75`); the session surfaces those issues as config notices rather than dropping them silently (`_runtime.py:2709-2715`).\n109: \n110: A declared hook that never fires is the failure mode to check first: an untrusted folder, a `type` Vibe rejected, or a duplicate name all leave the call unguarded while the run continues.\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: ## 4. PLUGIN CLASSIFICATION\n115: \n116: Vibe never imports or evaluates OpenCode's JavaScript or TypeScript plugins (`vibe/core/plugins/_foreign.py:310`, research section 6), so every plugin in `.opencode/plugins/` is re-expressed as a hook, a skill or nothing. The table classifies all 21; the verdict names the seam, and the reason sits in the row.\n117: \n118: | Plugin | What it does | Verdict | Vibe event |\n119: |---|---|---|---|\n120: | `system-spec-gate.js` | Classifies the operator prompt for file-mutation intent and denies a Write/Edit while the session gate is open and unanswered. | hook — a `pre_tool` hook never sees the prompt, so a `pre_agent` hook classifies it and persists the gate state the strict `pre_tool` half reads. A child session, marked by the inherited `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` or a parent id in the payload, is never denied | `pre_agent`, `pre_tool` (strict) |\n121: | `cli-dispatch-audit.js` | Denies a Bash dispatch that breaks a skill's hard rules, then appends one redacted audit line per completed dispatch. | hook | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n122: | `env-secret-guard.js` | Denies a call that would read or write a dotenv file, and registers three value-free dotenv inspection tools. | hook | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n123: | `overlay-guard.js` | Denies a write to a file a vendored tree's overlay owns and names the overlay file to edit instead. | hook | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n124: | `mcp-route-guard.js` | Logs a routing advisory when a native external MCP call has a Code Mode manual registered for its family; the port refuses the call instead of logging it. | hook | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n125: | `sk-git-message-gate.js` | Refuses a `git commit` message, `gh pr` description or branch name that breaks the repository's sk-git templates. | hook | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n126: | `system-deep-loop-guard.js` | Blocks a `task` dispatch to a deep-loop subagent whose declared mode disagrees with `mode-registry.json`, or a repeated loop-like dispatch. | hook — Vibe spawns subagents through `agents_spawn`, so the guard matches that tool and reads `tool_input.config_name` | `pre_tool` (strict) |\n127: | `sk-code-post-edit-quality.js` | Runs the post-edit quality router on each write and buffers the findings for the next system transform. | hook | `post_tool` (strict) |\n128: | `opencode-goal.js` | Keeps a session goal record, refreshes it on idle and injects the packet's goal slice into the system prompt. | hook | `session_start` |\n129: | `session-cleanup.js` | Runs the startup guards on session create and the cleanup script and process sweep on dispose. | hook — both lifecycle moments exist as host hooks | `session_start`, `session_end` |\n130: | `system-dist-freshness-guard.js` | Warns when a session or a risky Bash command is about to trust stale local dist outputs. | hook — `session_start` injects the warning as `additional_context`, and a non-strict `post_tool` entry adds the mid-session `STALE DIST WARNING` to the tool result after a write, edit or matched shell command (phase 015's keyed child run) | `session_start`, `post_tool` |\n131: | `system-skill-advisor.js` | Injects the skill advisor brief into each request's system text and exposes the advisor status tool. | hook — the `pre_agent` turn-start composer routes each main-session prompt through the shared advisor handler under the `vibe` label, so the brief arrives as `additional_context` (phase 015's keyed main-session run recorded `Advisor: no skill matched.`) | `pre_agent` |\n132: | `ask-surface-guard.js` | Reopens a finished turn when it closed with a prose option menu instead of the `question` tool. | hook — a non-strict `post_agent` part reads the finished turn through the journal reader and returns the prose menu once with the `ask_user_question` reprompt (phase 016's ten fixture cases; a live TUI retry stays operator-only) | `post_agent` |\n133: | `system-completion-sentinel.js` | Checks a turn's closing text for a completion claim and sends the evidence gap back to the model. | hook — a `post_agent` part records the gap as a pending advisory and the next turn's `pre_agent` composer delivers it once; the part never denies (phase 016's fixture suite and print-mode smoke run) | `post_agent`, `pre_agent` |\n134: | `session-handover.js` | Arms a relaunch near the context limit, writes a hand-off note and restarts the session under a supervisor. | hook, because Vibe's turn boundaries reach it: the `pre_agent` turn-start composer runs the context part last and the `post_tool` compaction binding runs it too, so at a turn start it expands a claim seed or withdraws an armed hand-over when the operator types, and at either event it nudges once the fill passes the threshold. The fill is the newest measured `input_tokens` in the session journal and the window is Vibe's `compaction_threshold`, which `SESSION_HANDOVER_WINDOW_TOKENS` overrides. The `post_agent` turn-end composer runs the arm part last, which arms a pending record and starts the killer and never denies. It ships off by default and `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_VIBE_ENABLED` turns it on, and an interactive Vibe exits 0 on the killer's SIGTERM. A hand-over the operator starts by typing `/speckit-handoff` prepares with a `uuidgen` id, is not armed and prints the claim command, while a nudged hand-over carries the real id and arms | `pre_agent`, `post_tool`, `post_agent` |\n135: | `classifier-injection-screen.js` | Screens fetched web text for instructions aimed at the agent and buffers an advisory for the next system transform. | hook — a non-strict `post_tool` hook on the fetch tool appends the advisory as `additional_context` to the result the model reads | `post_tool` |\n136: | `decision-capture.js` | Queues each answered `question` call as a decision record and nudges the next request toward `/speckit:save`. | hook — a non-strict `post_tool` adapter on `ask_user_question` queues each answer through the shared Vibe mapper, the save-time `sweep-vibe.mjs` replays the journal when the live hook did not fire, and the turn-start part reminds the model once per rising count; the live widget is interactive-only (phase 017's fixture suites) | `post_tool`, `pre_agent` |\n137: | `codex-hooks-watchdog.js` | Runs the Codex hook installer's `--check` at session start and logs drift in `~/.codex/hooks.json`. | not needed — it watches a file a Vibe session never reads | none |\n138: | `sk-git-preflight-advisory.js` | Evaluates Bash git commands against the sk-git rule engine and buffers up to three advisories for the next request. | not needed — the same rules are stated in sk-git's skill docs, and no tool hook can inject an advisory | none |\n139: | `system-speckit-completion.js` | Registers a read-only tool that returns a spec folder's level, checklist completion and placeholder percentage. | not needed — Vibe has no plugin tool registry, and the same payload comes from the spec-kit CLI the agent already runs | none |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 140]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-mistral-vibe/references/guards-and-hooks.md, lines 60-139\n60: `HookType` declares seven members (`models.py:20-27`). Three accept `strict` (`models.py:31-35`), and the model validator raises a `strict is only valid for ... hooks` error on any other type (`models.py:94-98`).\n61: \n62: | Type | `strict` | Fires | What it can decide |\n63: |---|---|---|---|\n64: | `pre_tool` | yes | Before a tool call | Refuse the call (`_foreign_hooks.py:14`). The only pre-execution seam a guard can use. |\n65: | `post_tool` | yes | After a tool call | Blank the tool result on a strict failure (`_foreign_hooks.py:15`); no run has shown it. |\n66: | `pre_agent` | yes | Before an agent turn | Block the message before the turn runs (`_foreign_hooks.py:16-17`). |\n67: | `post_agent` | no | After an agent turn | A deny sends a retry message the model answers, capped at three retries per turn; the fourth invocation is force-accepted. `strict` is rejected on a declared hook (`_foreign_hooks.py:18-20`), so the deny is the seam, not a held turn (phase 014 recorded `retry, retry, retry, accept`). |\n68: | `notification` | no | An approval or question opens; the main turn completes or fails | Nothing: it runs in the background and its output is ignored (`_host_hooks.py:6-8`). |\n69: | `session_start` | no | A session opens: `startup`, `resume`, `clear` or `fork` | Add `additional_context` to the session's next user message (`_host_hooks.py:9-12,65-83`). |\n70: | `session_end` | no | A session closes: `exit`, `clear` or `other` | Nothing: it runs in the background and its output is ignored (`_host_hooks.py:13-14`). |\n71: \n72: The last three are host hooks: the app server fires them outside the engine's turn (`models.py:37-42`). The first four are engine hooks, and only the engine hooks can refuse work.\n73: \n74: ### What `strict` Buys\n75: \n76: `strict` declares that a failing hook blocks instead of letting the call through. The validator enforces which types may carry it (`models.py:94-98`), and the harness runner's docstring maps a strict failure to a deny at `pre_tool`, a blanked result at `post_tool` and a blocked message at `pre_agent` (`mistralai_vibe_local_harness/vibe/_foreign_hooks.py:9-20`). `post_agent` rejects `strict`, but its conforming deny is not inert: Vibe returns the reason as a retry message, repeats the turn and force-accepts the fourth invocation. Phase 014's `DENY_MODE=always` fixture recorded `retry, retry, retry, accept`, and `turn_id` stayed the same on all four (`scratch/journal-excerpts/deny-always-hook-outcomes.jsonl`). That retry is the seam the turn-end composer uses (section 4), not a held turn. No run has shown a strict failure at any type; the `pre_tool` deny the wire fixture observed is a conforming deny.\n77: \n78: ### Protocols\n79: \n80: `HookProtocol` declares `vibe`, `claude_code` and `kimi_code` (`models.py:59-63`), so a Claude-format hook script is a candidate porting source. `protocol` is a runtime field on `RuntimeHookDefinition` (`models.py:113`), not a `HookConfig` field (`models.py:71-78`), and the default file loader ignores keys it does not model (`config.py:17-24`). A `protocol = \"claude_code\"` line in `hooks.toml` is therefore not how the protocol is selected; the loader or plugin that registers the hook sets it.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 3. DECLARATION AND LOADING\n85: \n86: ### The File\n87: \n88: A project declares hooks in `.vibe/hooks.toml` at the project root; discovery is root-only, like the rest of `.vibe/` ([runtime-folder-and-sync.md](./runtime-folder-and-sync.md) section 2). The file holds a `[[hooks]]` array (`config.py:17-24`), and each entry carries these fields (`models.py:71-78`):\n89: \n90: | Field | Required | Notes |\n91: |---|---|---|\n92: | `name` | yes | Unique across every loaded file; a duplicate