{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781131413,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14aaec10013XHBQRY6vR5ohn","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e14a8264001zf69mH3aFP0dkh","type":"tool","id":"call_3a135f2f8e7d4c5e86ac4629","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && grep -rn \"R3-P2-001\\|agents_spawn\\|match\" 032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md 032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md 032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md 2>/dev/null | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:3:description: \"Review pass five confirmed 2 P1 and 29 P2 findings on this branch. This phase fixes them in four lanes: the transcript scorer counts an in-place shell edit as a write, the arena builder refuses a dirty source or a stale build and records what it copied, the runner checks for a remote before every live turn, the kill-switch docs and tests name every switch name, the Vibe hook and the doctor read what they claim, and eight docs match the code. The stored arms are rescored, the fix is reviewed by Opus and re-reviewed by DeepSeek on its own diff.\"\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:55:- Kill-switch docs, a playbook control step and tests that name all ten switch names, and a lib README tree that matches the folder.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:56:- A Vibe part and a Claude hook that read what they claim, a doctor wiring check that reads `match`, and a hook contract that names Vibe.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:165:$ bash $PH/scratch/planning/wiring-match.sh .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs; echo \"exit=$?\"\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:166:match=agents_spawn ok vibe exit=0\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:167:match=main ok vibe exit=0\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:235:| `iter1-P2-quoted-command-line-is-a-start` | `COMMAND_LINE` matches anywhere in a line (`RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs:504-505`) | A marker counts only where it opens its line after list or emphasis markup, outside a quote or a fence (D4, T004) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:236:| `iter1-P2-mode-suffix-hides-repeat` | `commandLines` tallies the raw match (`:534-536`) | Tally on namespace and name through `commandParts` (D4, T005) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:250:| `R3-P2-001` | `tomlCommands` keeps only `type` and `command` (`DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs:233-254`) | Read `match`, and accept a `pre_agent` block only when it is absent or `main` (D9, T023) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:254:| `DM5-P2-001` | `SAD/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26` says 46 | 47 (T026) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:308:| `DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Modify | The `match` selector |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:309:| `DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` | Modify | The `match` cases |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:311:| `SAD/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` | Modify | 47 |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:343:| REQ-007 | The seven confirmed Vibe and doctor findings read fixed: `vibe-part.mjs` prints `directive-only changed: false`, a receipt follows the injected `env`, the Claude hook from source honors `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` prints `hook-missing vibe` for `match = \"agents_spawn\"`, the contract test is renamed and the hook contract names Vibe in its three places and says every alias silences every adapter. `R1-P2-002` is recorded as rejected. |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:360:- **SC-001**: `scratch/probes-after.txt` holds the after lines REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-005 and REQ-007 name, the `python write` line and the `remote-guard.mjs` lines equal to their before lines, and `wiring-match.sh` printing `match=agents_spawn hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml exit=1` and `match=main ok vibe exit=0`.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:414:<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Scope 6/25: one option in `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:35:- Lane D: `FM` is `$SAD/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`, `MTP` is `$PB/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `CL1` is `$SAD/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md`, `TRM` is `$ADV/tests/README.md`, `LS` is `$SAD/leaf-scopes.json`, `LM` is `$SAD/leaf-manifest.json` and `LA` is `$SAD/leaf-aliases.json`.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:43:- `PROBES` is, in this order: `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs`, `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs`, `node $V5/remote-guard.mjs`, `node $V5/vibe-part.mjs`, `bash $V5/arena-provenance.sh \"$PWD/$RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs\"`, `bash $SP/planning/arena-cases.sh \"$PWD/$RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs\"` and `bash $SP/planning/wiring-match.sh $HW`. Each writes nothing inside the repository and removes what it made. The arena probes print temporary heads and times, which differ per run and are compared by their other words only.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:45:- `LEFT` is `find \"${TMPDIR%/}\" -maxdepth 1 \\( -name 'arena-cases.*' -o -name 'wiring-match.*' -o -name 'probe-032.*' \\) | wc -l` and `find /tmp -maxdepth 1 \\( -name 'v5-arena-probe' -o -name 'v5-remote-probe' \\) | wc -l`, each of which must print 0 after a run. Each count is taken with `find`, never with an `ls` glob, because zsh aborts a command whose glob matches nothing.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:58:- When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:3:description: \"Review pass five confirmed 2 P1 and 29 P2 findings on this branch. This phase fixes them in four lanes: the transcript scorer counts an in-place shell edit as a write, the arena builder refuses a dirty source or a stale build and records what it copied, the runner checks for a remote before every live turn, the kill-switch docs and tests name every switch name, the Vibe hook and the doctor read what they claim, and eight docs match the code. The stored arms are rescored, the fix is reviewed by Opus and re-reviewed by DeepSeek on its own diff.\"\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:55:- Kill-switch docs, a playbook control step and tests that name all ten switch names, and a lib README tree that matches the folder.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:56:- A Vibe part and a Claude hook that read what they claim, a doctor wiring check that reads `match`, and a hook contract that names Vibe.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:165:$ bash $PH/scratch/planning/wiring-match.sh .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs; echo \"exit=$?\"\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:166:match=agents_spawn ok vibe exit=0\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:167:match=main ok vibe exit=0\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:235:| `iter1-P2-quoted-command-line-is-a-start` | `COMMAND_LINE` matches anywhere in a line (`RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs:504-505`) | A marker counts only where it opens its line after list or emphasis markup, outside a quote or a fence (D4, T004) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:236:| `iter1-P2-mode-suffix-hides-repeat` | `commandLines` tallies the raw match (`:534-536`) | Tally on namespace and name through `commandParts` (D4, T005) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:250:| `R3-P2-001` | `tomlCommands` keeps only `type` and `command` (`DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs:233-254`) | Read `match`, and accept a `pre_agent` block only when it is absent or `main` (D9, T023) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:254:| `DM5-P2-001` | `SAD/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26` says 46 | 47 (T026) |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:308:| `DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Modify | The `match` selector |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:309:| `DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` | Modify | The `match` cases |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:311:| `SAD/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` | Modify | 47 |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:343:| REQ-007 | The seven confirmed Vibe and doctor findings read fixed: `vibe-part.mjs` prints `directive-only changed: false`, a receipt follows the injected `env`, the Claude hook from source honors `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` prints `hook-missing vibe` for `match = \"agents_spawn\"`, the contract test is renamed and the hook contract names Vibe in its three places and says every alias silences every adapter. `R1-P2-002` is recorded as rejected. |\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:360:- **SC-001**: `scratch/probes-after.txt` holds the after lines REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-005 and REQ-007 name, the `python write` line and the `remote-guard.mjs` lines equal to their before lines, and `wiring-match.sh` printing `match=agents_spawn hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml exit=1` and `match=main ok vibe exit=0`.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:414:<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Scope 6/25: one option in `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:35:- Lane D: `FM` is `$SAD/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`, `MTP` is `$PB/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `CL1` is `$SAD/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md`, `TRM` is `$ADV/tests/README.md`, `LS` is `$SAD/leaf-scopes.json`, `LM` is `$SAD/leaf-manifest.json` and `LA` is `$SAD/leaf-aliases.json`.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:43:- `PROBES` is, in this order: `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs`, `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs`, `node $V5/remote-guard.mjs`, `node $V5/vibe-part.mjs`, `bash $V5/arena-provenance.sh \"$PWD/$RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs\"`, `bash $SP/planning/arena-cases.sh \"$PWD/$RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs\"` and `bash $SP/planning/wiring-match.sh $HW`. Each writes nothing inside the repository and removes what it made. The arena probes print temporary heads and times, which differ per run and are compared by their other words only.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:45:- `LEFT` is `find \"${TMPDIR%/}\" -maxdepth 1 \\( -name 'arena-cases.*' -o -name 'wiring-match.*' -o -name 'probe-032.*' \\) | wc -l` and `find /tmp -maxdepth 1 \\( -name 'v5-arena-probe' -o -name 'v5-remote-probe' \\) | wc -l`, each of which must print 0 after a run. Each count is taken with `find`, never with an `ls` glob, because zsh aborts a command whose glob matches nothing.\n032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:58:- When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && grep -rn \\\"R3-P2-001\\\\|agents_spawn\\\\|match\\\" 032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md 032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md 032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md 2>/dev/null | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781130433,"end":1794781131413}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781131520,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14aabce001ajjs4IuQtyCIpJ","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e14a8264001zf69mH3aFP0dkh","type":"tool","id":"call_b6d5a3f70d804c0e99da9463","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && grep -rn \"hook-wiring\\|skill-advisor-hook.md\\|match = \" --include=*.md . | grep -v \"review/\" | head -30","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"./014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:78:| `DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and their two tests | Modified | Flag-value refusal, the absent-entry repair line and the wiring matcher |\n./014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:115:| Wave 4 (T062 to T073) was added after the first verifier reports | It fixes what they flagged. That covers a stderr cap test that passed without the fix, the bench header, the hook-wiring matcher, the unguarded restore, a detached comment, the symlink status precedence, the symlink-blind entry guard, an arena comment, the Pi header read order, the raw id on a needs-a-mode head, the holdout empty-set guard and three README sentences |\n./014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:158:1. **The hook-wiring matcher misreads some shell shapes.** It reads `true; node <script>` and `cd x;node <script>` as missing and `echo 'x && node <script>'` as wired. It also reads `node --no-warnings <script>`, `/usr/bin/env node <script>` and `zsh -c 'node <script>'` as missing. No Skilled installer writes any of these shapes, so this is recorded and not built.\n./014-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:77:| AC-022 | REQ-022 | Given the symlink check workflow, When its output block is read, Then it names the hook check's exit 1 as WARN and exit 2 as FAIL | `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `rg -c \"hook-wiring check exits 1\" $DSC` prints 1. Met 2026-11-13: `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `rg -c \"hook-wiring check exits 1\" $DSC` prints 1. | Met | - |\n./014-review-remediation/tasks.md:37:- WG6: `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n./014-review-remediation/tasks.md:128:- [x] T036 Map the hook check's exits in the symlink output block (`DSC`). Add to `output`: `STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 0 and the hook-wiring check exits 1. Show each hook-missing line and the repair the step names.` and `STATUS=FAIL when the hook-wiring check exits 2. Quote its message.` Verify: `rg -c \"hook-wiring check exits 1\" $DSC` prints 1 and `NT $DS/tests/doctor-symlink-contract.test.cjs` reports `fail 0`.\n./014-review-remediation/tasks.md:167:- [x] T067 Say which status wins when the engine and the hook check disagree (`DSC`, `DSCT`). Test first: in `DSCT`, add one assertion to the case `the symlink output block maps the hook-wiring check exits to WARN and FAIL`: `assert.match(SYMLINK_CHECK.output, /When the engine and the hook-wiring check end on different statuses, the worse one wins: FAIL over WARN over OK\\./)`. Then add the line `When the engine and the hook-wiring check end on different statuses, the worse one wins: FAIL over WARN over OK.` as the last line of the `output: |` block in `DSC`, indented two spaces as the lines above it are. Verify: before the change `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 1`, after it `NT $DSCT` and `NT $DS/tests/doctor-symlink-contract.test.cjs` report `fail 0`.\n./014-review-remediation/plan.md:87:| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Feed `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:symlink check`, `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` and `command-offer.mjs` | update | T029 to T031 cases, `VO` for `codexHookApproval` |\n./014-review-remediation/spec.md:220:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` and their tests | Modify | Flag value refusal, absent repair line, command-entry marker match |\n./014-review-remediation/spec.md:266:| REQ-020 | `DR5-P2-002`: `hook-wiring-check.cjs` reports `ok` only when a `type: command` entry's `command` runs `node` on the runtime's hook script, and a marker in any other field reads `hook-missing`. |\n./026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:137:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:169-173` | `:169-173` | Lines match. The names there are `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_*_DISABLED` and the `SPECKIT_` legacy aliases. The report's `SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` and `SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` are read by nothing |\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:34:- Lane V: `VB` is `$SAD/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs`, `VBT` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/vibe-prompt-advisor.vitest.ts`, `UPS` is `$SAD/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`, `UPT` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/claude-user-prompt-submit-hook.vitest.ts`, `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `HWT` is `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `RMC` is `$DS/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs` and `HK` is `$SAD/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:130:- [x] T023 Read the Vibe `match` selector in the doctor's wiring check (`HWT`, then `HW`). After T022. Test first, in `HWT`, with the `vibeBlock` and `writeVibeHooks` helpers extended to take an optional match line: a `pre_agent` block with `match = \"agents_spawn\"` prints `hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml`, one with `match = \"re:main|other\"` prints the same, one with `match = \"main\"` prints `ok vibe`, and the existing block with no match still prints `ok vibe`. Run `node --test $HWT` and see the `agents_spawn` case print `ok vibe`. Then keep `match` in `tomlCommands`'s blocks and accept a Vibe `pre_agent` block in `inspect` only when `match` is absent or exactly `main`, as `plan.md` D9 states. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `node --test $HWT` reports `fail 0`, `bash $SP/planning/wiring-match.sh $HW` prints `match=agents_spawn hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml exit=1` and `match=main ok vibe exit=0`, and `node $HW --root . | rg vibe` prints `ok vibe`. Evidence: first run fail 2 on ok vibe for agents_spawn and re:, then tests 47 fail 0, wiring-match agents_spawn hook-missing and main ok, repo ok vibe, typecheck 0. The Opus verifier rejected the fail-open read of an unparsed match line (single quotes, trailing comment), fixed in T023a\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:131:- [x] T023a Read every Vibe match line the doctor sees (`HWT`, then `HW`). After T023, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T023. Test first, in `HWT`: a `pre_agent` block with `match = 'agents_spawn'` and one with `match = \"agents_spawn\"  # subagents` each print `hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml`, and one with `match = 'main'` prints `ok vibe`. Run `node --test $HWT` and see the two `agents_spawn` cases print `ok vibe`. Then in `tomlCommands` read a `match` value written as a basic or a literal string with an optional trailing comment, and record any other `match` line in a block as a selector that is not `main`, so `inspect` reads it as `hook-missing`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `node --test $HWT` reports `fail 0`, `bash $SP/planning/wiring-match.sh $HW` prints `match=agents_spawn hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml exit=1` and `match=main ok vibe exit=0`, and `node $HW --root . | rg vibe` prints `ok vibe`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T023a.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:147:**Decision.** `skillAdvisorHookEnabled` in `SAD/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` finds `hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs` by walking up from its own folder, as `loadHookFlags` in `ADV/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:50-68` does, and keeps its fail-open answer. `tomlCommands` in `DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` keeps `match` beside `type` and `command`, and `inspect` accepts a block for the Vibe `pre_agent` event only when `match` is absent or exactly `main`. Any other value, `re:` selectors included, reads `hook-missing`.\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:149:**Why.** The walk-up already exists for the same resolver in the same skill. A `re:` selector could match the main agent or not, and the doctor cannot run Vibe's matcher, so it reports what it can prove. The real `.vibe/hooks.toml` uses `match = \"main\"` (line 18), so it still reads `ok vibe`.\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:215:| `tomlCommands`, `inspect` (`DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs:233`, `:350`) | The doctor's Vibe row | update (T023) | `HWT`, the `agents_spawn` probe |\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:165:$ bash $PH/scratch/planning/wiring-match.sh .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs; echo \"exit=$?\"\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:169:$ node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root . | grep vibe\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:250:| `R3-P2-001` | `tomlCommands` keeps only `type` and `command` (`DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs:233-254`) | Read `match`, and accept a `pre_agent` block only when it is absent or `main` (D9, T023) |\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:252:| `R2-P2-002`, `R3-P2-002` | `SAD/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:173` and `:175` split the aliases by adapter. `:3`, `:84` and the start table at `:102-112` omit Vibe | Every alias silences every adapter and the direct call, and Vibe joins all three places (T025) |\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:307:| `SAD/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` | Modify | The alias rows and Vibe |\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:308:| `DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Modify | The `match` selector |\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:309:| `DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` | Modify | The `match` cases |\n./032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:343:| REQ-007 | The seven confirmed Vibe and doctor findings read fixed: `vibe-part.mjs` prints `directive-only changed: false`, a receipt follows the injected `env`, the Claude hook from source honors `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` prints `hook-missing vibe` for `match = \"agents_spawn\"`, the contract test is renamed and the hook contract names Vibe in its three places and says every alias silences every adapter. `R1-P2-002` is recorded as rejected. |\n./003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md:107:| Six advisor documents (`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `README.md`, `hooks/lib/README.md`, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`, the two feature-catalog entries) and other advisor READMEs | Modified | The hook's route request described as it now is |\n./017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:74:- **WG9, doctor checks.** `hook-wiring-check.cjs` splits a command into simple commands outside quotes and reads `env`, `bash`, `sh` and `zsh` wrappers. A10 counts only `PASS` copies as expected and names report-only copies apart.\n./017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:95:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `agents-md-check.cjs`, `tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` | Modified | Quote-aware launch reader, A10 count (WG9) |\n./017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:176:7. **The `sh` shell has no hook-wiring case of its own.** `bash` and `zsh` have cases, and the reader checks all three names from one list.\n./017-review-pass-two-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:82:| AC-027 | REQ-027 | Given the seven wrapper launches and a quoted `echo` of the script, When the hook-wiring check reads them, Then the launches read `ok` and the `echo` reads `hook-missing` | The T034 cases pass in `NT $HWT`, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok` for claude, codex, cursor and devin, and