{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781159740,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14b1f2b001zaXuOSMpYXxVsF","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e14ab80d001cCIOfIuEkntmEs","type":"tool","id":"call_f2286a8422da4a5084a700f4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","offset":178,"limit":30},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 178-207\n178: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n179: | `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`. Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n180: | `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output, and the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstains. |\n181: | `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n182: | `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n183: \n184: The direct call decides in the caller's own process, by the same resolution the adapters use. `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` asks `hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor')` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs`, with the caller's environment over `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`, before it connects to a daemon or runs the local scorer. Whenever the adapters are off, under any name in this table or its older `MK_` form, any truthy value or a line in the flags file, it prints the empty envelope with `ADVISOR_DISABLED` and names the switch that decided. A daemon reads the same names from its own environment and never reads the flags file, and the launcher passes no switch name and no `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` to a daemon it starts, so a flagged command that happens to start the daemon does not leave it abstaining for every later caller. The standalone Python CLI keeps its own rule: only `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, set to exactly `1`.\n185: \n186: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (kept for existing configs: the transform adds no compiled-route line, so it changes only the `bounded_compiled_route_summary` status field).\n187: \n188: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n193: \n194: | Boundary | Rule |\n195: |---|---|\n196: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n197: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n198: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n199: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n200: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n201: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n202: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n203: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n204: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n205: \n206: ### Operator freshness states\n207: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 208]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 178-207\n178: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n179: | `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`. Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n180: | `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output, and the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstains. |\n181: | `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n182: | `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Older alias of `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n183: \n184: The direct call decides in the caller's own process, by the same resolution the adapters use. `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` asks `hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor')` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs`, with the caller's environment over `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`, before it connects to a daemon or runs the local scorer. Whenever the adapters are off, under any name in this table or its older `MK_` form, any truthy value or a line in the flags file, it prints the empty envelope with `ADVISOR_DISABLED` and names the switch that decided. A daemon reads the same names from its own environment and never reads the flags file, and the launcher passes no switch name and no `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` to a daemon it starts, so a flagged command that happens to start the daemon does not leave it abstaining for every later caller. The standalone Python CLI keeps its own rule: only `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, set to exactly `1`.\n185: \n186: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (kept for existing configs: the transform adds no compiled-route line, so it changes only the `bounded_compiled_route_summary` status field).\n187: \n188: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n193: \n194: | Boundary | Rule |\n195: |---|---|\n196: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n197: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n198: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n199: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n200: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n201: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n202: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n203: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n204: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n205: \n206: ### Operator freshness states\n207: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 208]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"offset\":178,\"limit\":30}"},"time":{"start":1794781159211,"end":1794781159740}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781159764,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14b1ced001NLlMzYo6e9vRIb","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e14ab80d001cCIOfIuEkntmEs","type":"tool","id":"call_c726fc0f1b9f4b40be3756f2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '30,90p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. HELPERS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ntype PublicThresholds = AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'];\n\ninterface HookFlagsResolver {\n  hookFlagDecision(\n    concern: string,\n    env?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv,\n    config?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>,\n  ): { enabled: boolean; key: string | null };\n  loadConfigFile(path: string): Record<string, string>;\n  configPath(): string;\n  concernFlag(concern: string): string | null;\n  MASTER_FLAG: string;\n  MASTER_ALIASES: readonly string[];\n  LEGACY_ALIASES: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n}\n\n// The source and the built module sit at different depths below .skilled, so the\n// resolver is found by walking up rather than by counting parent hops. A missing\n// resolver answers as if no switch were set, as every adapter does.\nfunction loadHookFlags(): HookFlagsResolver | null {\n  let folder = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n  while (true) {\n    const resolverPath = join(folder, 'hooks', 'shared', 'hook-flags.cjs');\n    if (existsSync(resolverPath)) {\n      try {\n        return createRequire(import.meta.url)(resolverPath) as HookFlagsResolver;\n      } catch {\n        return null;\n      }\n    }\n    const parent = dirname(folder);\n    if (parent === folder) return null;\n    folder = parent;\n  }\n}\n\nconst hookFlags = loadHookFlags();\nconst skillAdvisorFlag = hookFlags?.concernFlag('skill-advisor') ?? null;\n\n// Callers strip these names to isolate a scope from a switch set in the shell.\nexport const ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS: readonly string[] = hookFlags === null\n  ? []\n  : [\n      hookFlags.MASTER_FLAG,\n      ...hookFlags.MASTER_ALIASES,\n      ...(skillAdvisorFlag === null ? [] : [skillAdvisorFlag]),\n      ...(hookFlags.LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor'] ?? []),\n    ];\n\n// Both arguments go in so an explicit environment never drops the file. The file\n// is read per call because each CLI call is its own process.\nexport function advisorDisabledBy(\n  env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env,\n  config?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>,\n): string | null {\n  if (hookFlags === null) return null;\n  const fileConfig = config ?? hookFlags.loadConfigFile(env.HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG || hookFlags.configPath());\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. HELPERS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ntype PublicThresholds = AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'];\n\ninterface HookFlagsResolver {\n  hookFlagDecision(\n    concern: string,\n    env?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv,\n    config?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>,\n  ): { enabled: boolean; key: string | null };\n  loadConfigFile(path: string): Record<string, string>;\n  configPath(): string;\n  concernFlag(concern: string): string | null;\n  MASTER_FLAG: string;\n  MASTER_ALIASES: readonly string[];\n  LEGACY_ALIASES: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n}\n\n// The source and the built module sit at different depths below .skilled, so the\n// resolver is found by walking up rather than by counting parent hops. A missing\n// resolver answers as if no switch were set, as every adapter does.\nfunction loadHookFlags(): HookFlagsResolver | null {\n  let folder = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n  while (true) {\n    const resolverPath = join(folder, 'hooks', 'shared', 'hook-flags.cjs');\n    if (existsSync(resolverPath)) {\n      try {\n        return createRequire(import.meta.url)(resolverPath) as HookFlagsResolver;\n      } catch {\n        return null;\n      }\n    }\n    const parent = dirname(folder);\n    if (parent === folder) return null;\n    folder = parent;\n  }\n}\n\nconst hookFlags = loadHookFlags();\nconst skillAdvisorFlag = hookFlags?.concernFlag('skill-advisor') ?? null;\n\n// Callers strip these names to isolate a scope from a switch set in the shell.\nexport const ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS: readonly string[] = hookFlags === null\n  ? []\n  : [\n      hookFlags.MASTER_FLAG,\n      ...hookFlags.MASTER_ALIASES,\n      ...(skillAdvisorFlag === null ? [] : [skillAdvisorFlag]),\n      ...(hookFlags.LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor'] ?? []),\n    ];\n\n// Both arguments go in so an explicit environment never drops the file. The file\n// is read per call because each CLI call is its own process.\nexport function advisorDisabledBy(\n  env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env,\n  config?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>,\n): string | null {\n  if (hookFlags === null) return null;\n  const fileConfig = config ?? hookFlags.loadConfigFile(env.HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG || hookFlags.configPath());\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '30,90p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781158637,"end":1794781159764}}}}
