{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781419710,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14f023b001Mye92RLQSyGYT9","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e14ee9e0001ohxB8kj9xotkpd","type":"tool","id":"call_b80544a1ce22426c9d87fefd","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[Populated after iteration 1]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[Populated after iteration 1]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Running the exported `withCommandDocuments` and `reduceRepeatedHead` instead of reading them:\n  the fallback guard and the receipt environment each print one observable (`changed: false`;\n  `injected 1 / process 0`), so the two fixes are confirmed rather than inferred (iteration 1).\n- Comparing the new resolver walk with the old six-hop URL from both the source and the built\n  folder: the source misses the old path and the built folder hits it, which is exactly the\n  reported asymmetry, and the walk resolves both (iteration 1).\n- Reading the new hook test for what it can only pass with: a missing resolver answers enabled,\n  so `{}` plus an uncalled producer proves the walk found the file, not the fail-open branch\n  (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading the unbounded resolver walk as a new defect failed: plan D9 freezes the walk-up and\n  `advisor-disabled.ts:50-68` is the same loop, so a finding would re-open a decided tradeoff\n  without a new input (iteration 1).\n- Reading the compiled runtime as the reviewed artifact failed: it is untracked and rebuilt, so\n  the TypeScript source is the review target and the working-tree copy is only corroboration\n  (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -97,15 +97,28 @@\n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[Populated after iteration 1]\n+- Running the exported `withCommandDocuments` and `reduceRepeatedHead` instead of reading them:\n+  the fallback guard and the receipt environment each print one observable (`changed: false`;\n+  `injected 1 / process 0`), so the two fixes are confirmed rather than inferred (iteration 1).\n+- Comparing the new resolver walk with the old six-hop URL from both the source and the built\n+  folder: the source misses the old path and the built folder hits it, which is exactly the\n+  reported asymmetry, and the walk resolves both (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the new hook test for what it can only pass with: a missing resolver answers enabled,\n+  so `{}` plus an uncalled producer proves the walk found the file, not the fail-open branch\n+  (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[Populated after iteration 1]\n+- Reading the unbounded resolver walk as a new defect failed: plan D9 freezes the walk-up and\n+  `advisor-disabled.ts:50-68` is the same loop, so a finding would re-open a decided tradeoff\n+  without a new input (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the compiled runtime as the reviewed artifact failed: it is untracked and rebuilt, so\n+  the TypeScript source is the review target and the working-tree copy is only corroboration\n+  (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n","status":"modified","additions":15,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[Populated after iteration 1]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[Populated after iteration 1]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Running the exported `withCommandDocuments` and `reduceRepeatedHead` instead of reading them:\\n  the fallback guard and the receipt environment each print one observable (`changed: false`;\\n  `injected 1 / process 0`), so the two fixes are confirmed rather than inferred (iteration 1).\\n- Comparing the new resolver walk with the old six-hop URL from both the source and the built\\n  folder: the source misses the old path and the built folder hits it, which is exactly the\\n  reported asymmetry, and the walk resolves both (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the new hook test for what it can only pass with: a missing resolver answers enabled,\\n  so `{}` plus an uncalled producer proves the walk found the file, not the fail-open branch\\n  (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Reading the unbounded resolver walk as a new defect failed: plan D9 freezes the walk-up and\\n  `advisor-disabled.ts:50-68` is the same loop, so a finding would re-open a decided tradeoff\\n  without a new input (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the compiled runtime as the reviewed artifact failed: it is untracked and rebuilt, so\\n  the TypeScript source is the review target and the working-tree copy is only corroboration\\n  (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781413947,"end":1794781419710}}}}
