eage's scope. Their five focus checks are read here only as context, never graded.\n61: - The kill-switch CLI, launcher and `ENV-REFERENCE.md` are the `kill-switch-cli` lineage's\n62:   scope. The hook contract is graded here only where it describes this area's code.\n63: - The feature catalog, changelog, playbook and leaf metadata are `docs-metadata`'s scope.\n64: - Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to filename searches.\n65: - No code changes. This lineage writes only its own directory.\n66: \n67: ---\n68: \n69: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n70: \n71: - Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below 0.10 with no active P0 and dimension coverage complete.\n72: - Cap: `maxIterations` 3.\n73: - Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence.\n74: - Any active P0 forces `Review verdict: FAIL` regardless of convergence.\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n79: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n80: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n81: [None yet]\n82: \n83: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n88: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n89: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n90: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n91: - P1 (Required): 0\n92: - P2 (Suggestions): 0\n93: - Resolved: 0\n94: \n95: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n100: \n101: - Running the exported `withCommandDocuments` and `reduceRepeatedHead` instead of reading them:\n102:   the fallback guard and the receipt environment each print one observable (`changed: false`;\n103:   `injected 1 / process 0`), so the two fixes are confirmed rather than inferred (iteration 1).\n104: - Comparing the new resolver walk with the old six-hop URL from both the source and the built\n105:   folder: the source misses the old path and the built folder hits it, which is exactly the\n106:   reported asymmetry, and the walk resolves both (iteration 1).\n107: - Reading the new hook test for what it can only pass with: a missing resolver answers enabled,\n108:   so `{}` plus an uncalled producer proves the walk found the file, not the fail-open branch\n109:   (iteration 1).\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n114: \n115: - Reading the unbounded resolver walk as a new defect failed: plan D9 freezes the walk-up and\n116:   `advisor-disabled.ts:50-68` is the same loop, so a finding would re-open a decided tradeoff\n117:   without a new input (iteration 1).\n118: - Reading the compiled runtime as the reviewed artifact failed: it is untracked and rebuilt, so\n119:   the TypeScript source is the review target and the working-tree copy is only corroboration\n120:   (iteration 1).\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n125: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n126: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n127: [No exhausted approach categories yet]\n128: \n129: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n134: - Completed pivots: 0\n135: - Failed pivots: 0\n136: - Audited overrides: 0\n137: - Swept: none yet\n138: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n139: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n140: \n141: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n142: \n143: - **The unbounded ancestor walk loads a foreign resolver.** Ruled out as a finding: plan D9\n144:   freezes the walk-up, `advisor-disabled.ts:50-68` is the identical sibling, and no in-repo\n145:   caller places a `hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs` above a checkout (iteration 1).\n146: - **The directive-only early return skips a real head.** Ruled out: the handler's no-brief\n147:   fallback is the only context that opens with `Directives:`, and a headed brief opens with\n148:   `Advisor:` (iteration 1).\n149: - **A missing resolver now fails closed.** Ruled out: null answers enabled, the same fail-open\n150:   answer the old catch gave (iteration 1).\n151: \n152: ---\n153: \n154: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n155: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n156