{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781506845,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e15069f40011OgdND76Nadbq2","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e15053c2001CV14umeS9w4NUx","type":"tool","id":"call_c9641663bf8f49918b5b46ad","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":14,"offset":228,"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown, lines 228-241\n228: | `git-standards.cjs` | `status` and `check` are read-only. `init`, `set` and `disable` are dry runs until `--apply`, which writes only `.sk-git/` or the `skgit.contractDir` directory, never the shipped sk-git templates. |\n229: | `git-setup-check.cjs` | Read-only. It writes no file and no git config value, and calls no allocator or `--apply` mode. |\n230: | `sk-code-quality-config.cjs` | `status` and `check` are read-only; `status` starts the runner's `--explain` once per batch of up to 500 sampled paths and no configured check. `init` is a dry run until `--apply`, which creates only `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` and refuses with `CONFIG_EXISTS` when that file exists. |\n231: | `agents-md-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root: it reads the instruction file, its runtime copies and `REPO RULES.md`, runs three owner tools as children in their check-only forms and writes nothing. |\n232: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n233: | `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n234: | `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n235: | `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime's entry runs its hook script, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. Its Vibe reading is line by line, so a `.vibe/hooks.toml` that Vibe cannot parse can still read `ok vibe`, and a value with a trailing comment or a single-quoted string reads `hook-missing`. |\n236: | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | The battery itself writes only the `--out` file and temporary folders it removes when each step ends. The private server's folder is also removed on `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, and the server is stopped. The import check runs each plugin's v1 factory in a child process rooted at the repository, so anything a plugin does when it loads happens during the check. It never touches the shared v2 service and never prints the private server's password. OpenCode 1 writes into a temporary data folder, not the user's. |\n237: \n238: Do not invoke a mutating path from a route classified as read-only.\n239: \n240: ---\n241: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 242]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown, lines 228-241\n228: | `git-standards.cjs` | `status` and `check` are read-only. `init`, `set` and `disable` are dry runs until `--apply`, which writes only `.sk-git/` or the `skgit.contractDir` directory, never the shipped sk-git templates. |\n229: | `git-setup-check.cjs` | Read-only. It writes no file and no git config value, and calls no allocator or `--apply` mode. |\n230: | `sk-code-quality-config.cjs` | `status` and `check` are read-only; `status` starts the runner's `--explain` once per batch of up to 500 sampled paths and no configured check. `init` is a dry run until `--apply`, which creates only `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` and refuses with `CONFIG_EXISTS` when that file exists. |\n231: | `agents-md-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root: it reads the instruction file, its runtime copies and `REPO RULES.md`, runs three owner tools as children in their check-only forms and writes nothing. |\n232: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n233: | `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | `--check` is read-only. `--write` rewrites the manifest's `derived` key and refuses to run outside the repository that ships the template. |\n234: | `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It reads `.codex/hooks.json` and the Codex config, prints no hash and takes no write path. It exits 0 on a skip or an approval, 1 on a missing or unapproved entry and 2 on a bad argument. |\n235: | `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root. It writes no file and runs no installer, and its JSON form reports the same readings as its lines. It exits 0 when every installed runtime's entry runs its hook script, 1 when one is missing and 2 on a bad argument or a missing root. Its Vibe reading is line by line, so a `.vibe/hooks.toml` that Vibe cannot parse can still read `ok vibe`, and a value with a trailing comment or a single-quoted string reads `hook-missing`. |\n236: | `opencode-version-battery.cjs` | The battery itself writes only the `--out` file and temporary folders it removes when each step ends. The private server's folder is also removed on `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, and the server is stopped. The import check runs each plugin's v1 factory in a child process rooted at the repository, so anything a plugin does when it loads happens during the check. It never touches the shared v2 service and never prints the private server's password. OpenCode 1 writes into a temporary data folder, not the user's. |\n237: \n238: Do not invoke a mutating path from a route classified as read-only.\n239: \n240: ---\n241: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 242]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":14,\"offset\":228,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781506036,"end":1794781506845}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781506850,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1506b80001AmbTIT4vlICJNV","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e15053c2001CV14umeS9w4NUx","type":"tool","id":"call_0547e2772c274983b71ee8ca","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":45,"offset":232,"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs, lines 232-276\n232:   });\n233:   const result = f.run();\n234:   assert.equal(result.code, 1);\n235:   assert.match(result.out, /^hook-missing claude \\.claude\\/settings\\.json$/m);\n236: });\n237: \n238: // Vibe keeps its hooks in TOML and only a `pre_agent` entry for the main agent\n239: // that starts node on the turn-start script runs before the prompt, so each\n240: // shape below must not count.\n241: test('passes the Vibe turn-start entry under pre_agent', (t) => {\n242:   const f = fixture(t);\n243:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"'));\n244:   const text = f.run();\n245:   assert.equal(text.code, 0);\n246:   assert.equal(text.out.trim(), 'ok vibe');\n247: });\n248: \n249: test('passes a Vibe entry whose match selector names the main agent', (t) => {\n250:   const f = fixture(t);\n251:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"', 'match = \"main\"'));\n252:   const text = f.run();\n253:   assert.equal(text.code, 0);\n254:   assert.equal(text.out.trim(), 'ok vibe');\n255: });\n256: \n257: test('passes a Vibe entry with no match line', (t) => {\n258:   const f = fixture(t);\n259:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"', null));\n260:   const text = f.run();\n261:   assert.equal(text.code, 0);\n262:   assert.equal(text.out.trim(), 'ok vibe');\n263: });\n264: \n265: test('names Vibe when its turn-start entry matches another agent', (t) => {\n266:   const f = fixture(t);\n267:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"'), 'match = \"agents_spawn\"');\n268:   const result = f.run();\n269:   assert.equal(result.code, 1, result.out.trim());\n270:   assert.match(result.out, /^hook-missing vibe \\.vibe\\/hooks\\.toml$/m);\n271: });\n272: \n273: test('names Vibe when its match selector is a regular expression', (t) => {\n274:   const f = fixture(t);\n275:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"', 'match = \"re:main|other\"'));\n276:   const result = f.run();\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 277]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs, lines 232-276\n232:   });\n233:   const result = f.run();\n234:   assert.equal(result.code, 1);\n235:   assert.match(result.out, /^hook-missing claude \\.claude\\/settings\\.json$/m);\n236: });\n237: \n238: // Vibe keeps its hooks in TOML and only a `pre_agent` entry for the main agent\n239: // that starts node on the turn-start script runs before the prompt, so each\n240: // shape below must not count.\n241: test('passes the Vibe turn-start entry under pre_agent', (t) => {\n242:   const f = fixture(t);\n243:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"'));\n244:   const text = f.run();\n245:   assert.equal(text.code, 0);\n246:   assert.equal(text.out.trim(), 'ok vibe');\n247: });\n248: \n249: test('passes a Vibe entry whose match selector names the main agent', (t) => {\n250:   const f = fixture(t);\n251:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"', 'match = \"main\"'));\n252:   const text = f.run();\n253:   assert.equal(text.code, 0);\n254:   assert.equal(text.out.trim(), 'ok vibe');\n255: });\n256: \n257: test('passes a Vibe entry with no match line', (t) => {\n258:   const f = fixture(t);\n259:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"', null));\n260:   const text = f.run();\n261:   assert.equal(text.code, 0);\n262:   assert.equal(text.out.trim(), 'ok vibe');\n263: });\n264: \n265: test('names Vibe when its turn-start entry matches another agent', (t) => {\n266:   const f = fixture(t);\n267:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"'), 'match = \"agents_spawn\"');\n268:   const result = f.run();\n269:   assert.equal(result.code, 1, result.out.trim());\n270:   assert.match(result.out, /^hook-missing vibe \\.vibe\\/hooks\\.toml$/m);\n271: });\n272: \n273: test('names Vibe when its match selector is a regular expression', (t) => {\n274:   const f = fixture(t);\n275:   writeVibeHooks(f.root, vibeBlock('pre_agent', 'command = \"' + VIBE_COMMAND + '\"', 'match = \"re:main|other\"'));\n276:   const result = f.run();\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 277]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":45,\"offset\":232,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781506432,"end":1794781506850}}}}
