{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781579343,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e151318b001h02EuTt6MmnrXX","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e150ded8001avRFp0ql0iTuFy","type":"tool","id":"call_0c7be26e26904a429a90351b","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002 - traceability and maintainability\n\nLineage: `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b`. Iteration 2 of 3. Mode: review.\nExecutor: this session, `cli-opencode` model `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Second iteration of the confirming round for the `vibe-hooks-doctor` area. State read first:\n  `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-strategy.md`,\n  `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, and `review/review-scope-5b.txt` for the area mapping.\n- `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory at this iteration.\n- The operator focus's doctor item (\"the doctor hooks-file reading\") and its docs item (\"docs\n  agree with code\") are addressed here. The five `accuracy-runner` checks stay out of scope by\n  `review-scope-5b.txt` and are not graded.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:40-77,110-200,227-273,367-393`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:39-63,238-310`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs:60-90,119-160,203-209`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:104-115,228-236`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/vibe-command-documents.md:16-36,126-143`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:250,343` and `acceptance-criteria.md:62`\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe -- <the doctor script and its two tests>`\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The doctor README's Vibe sentence is false after the selector fix** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235` -- The row says \"a value with a trailing comment or a single-quoted string reads `hook-missing`\". Since `tomlCommands` now parses a `match` value as a basic or a literal string with an optional trailing comment (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:235-245,268-269`), a `match` value written in either shape reads `ok vibe`. The same row at `README.markdown:112` describes the Vibe reading without the new selector rule, so an operator whose `pre_agent` entry carries any other selector sees `hook-missing` and no describing doc explains it.\n   Case: a `.vibe/hooks.toml` turn-start block written `match = 'main'`, or `match = \"main\"  # main agent only`, reads `ok vibe` with exit 0, while `README.markdown:235` says that shape reads `hook-missing`.\n   Finding class: documentation_contract\n   Scope proof: the README is the describing doc for the in-scope script; no other file states this sentence, and the script's own comments state the opposite rule.\n   Affected surface hints: the doctor scripts README rows 112 and 235, and the operator repair path for a `hook-missing vibe` line.\n2. **The new \"names the main agent\" case duplicates the default case, so it cannot fail for a reason of its own** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249-255` -- `vibeBlock`'s third parameter defaults to `match = \"main\"` (`:54`), so the new case writes byte-identical TOML to the case at `:241-247` and asserts the same exit code and line. The explicit-selector branch is already exercised by the default, so the added case can only fail when the older case fails too.\n   Case: change `vibeBlock`'s default to `match = \"agents_spawn\"` and the two cases fail together; the new test never distinguishes an explicit selector from the default one.\n   Finding class: test_hygiene\n   Scope proof: both cases and the helper are in the in-scope test file; the sibling cases at `:257-271` and `:273-303` cover the absent and non-`main` branches.\n   Affected surface hints: the doctor wiring suite's case list and the \"names the main agent\" title.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- **`spec_code` (core): partial.** Phase `032` REQ-007's doctor item is \"`hook-wiring-check.cjs`\n  prints `hook-missing vibe` for `match = \"agents_spawn\"`\". A fixture with that selector printed\n  `hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml` and exit 1, and the repository's own file printed\n  `ok vibe` and exit 0, so the requirement holds. The same row's doc item covers\n  `skill-advisor-hook.md`, not the doctor README, so finding 1 is a describing-doc gap rather\n  than a contradicted requirement.\n- **`checklist_evidence` (core): partial.** Phase `032` AC-007 names the same cases and all of\n  them pass at this commit, including the contract-test rename and the `agents_spawn` refusal.\n  The packet's AC row still reads `Unmet`; that is the phase's own close-out state and is\n  recorded under Edge Cases, not graded here.\n- **`skill_agent` (overlay): notApplicable.** No agent definition changed in this area.\n- **`agent_cross_runtime` (overlay): pass.** The check covers five runtime files and the fix\n  touches only the Vibe row; the other four readings are unchanged (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:40-77`)\n  and the repository run prints `ok` for all five.\n- **`feature_catalog_code` (overlay): notApplicable here.** Feature-catalog text is the\n  `docs-metadata` area by `review-scope-5b.txt`.\n- **`playbook_capability` (overlay): pass.** `CL-010` claims the document line after the head and\n  an empty child-session result; iteration 1's probe printed exactly those, and no playbook\n  covers the doctor check.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The doctor script reads the same `.vibe/hooks.toml` the runtime loads: the repository file's\n  turn-start block carries `match = \"main\"` and the check prints `ok vibe`, so the selector rule\n  is exercised against the shipped wiring rather than a fixture alone.\n- The contract test's renamed case walks `MIRROR_CHECKS = [...DSH_CHECKS, ...VIBE_CHECKS]` and\n  asserts `node <script> --check` for each (`doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs:88,119-137,203-205`),\n  so its new title names exactly what it proves.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Phase `032`'s `acceptance-criteria.md:62` (AC-007) still reads `Unmet` while every item it names\n  passes at this commit. The confirm round is not the phase close-out, so this is recorded as\n  bookkeeping for the coordinator and not raised as a finding.\n- The doctor README also describes the `--json` form; the fixture runs used the line form. Both\n  forms share `inspect`, so the selector rule is the same, and the JSON form was not separately\n  exercised.\n- `re:` selectors read `hook-missing` by design (plan D9, pinned by the case at\n  `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:273-280`). Not re-reported.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The selector rule matches plan D9 exactly: absent → `ok vibe`; `main` as a basic or literal\n  string, with or without a trailing comment → `ok vibe`; any other value → `hook-missing vibe`\n  (four fixtures, plus the repository's own file).\n- An unparsable `match` line becomes a selector naming no agent, so a line the reader cannot\n  parse narrows the match instead of widening it (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:238-245,268-269`).\n- The block filter still requires the block's `type` to be the runtime's event and its `command`\n  to be a string, so a `match` line cannot lend an entry to another event\n  (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:271-272`).\n- `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` printed\n  `tests 50`, `pass 50`, `fail 0`, exit 0.\n- The renamed contract test is accurate: `routeGaps` iterates both runtime check lists and\n  enforces `node` plus `--check`, which is what \"every DSH and Vibe check in its check-only form\"\n  means (`doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs:88,119-137`).\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .` still prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor`, `ok devin`,\n  `ok vibe` and exits 0, so the fix did not break the shipped wiring.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A `re:` selector that includes `main` is falsely reported.** Not raised: plan D9 decides that\n  any value other than absent or exactly `main` reads `hook-missing`, \"`re:` selectors\n  included\", and the case at `:273-280` pins the decision. Re-reporting it would need a new\n  input that D9 does not already answer.\n- **The three added cases after T023 make the suite count wrong.** T023's evidence says 47 tests\n  and the suite now prints 50; T023a added three `match` cases, so the count is consistent with\n  the task record and no case is unaccounted for.\n- **A trailing-comment `type` or `command` line is now accepted.** Still refused: the entry regex\n  anchors on the closing quote with no comment (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:263`), and the README's\n  sentence stays true for those two keys. Only `match` gained comment tolerance.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability and traceability\n- Focus area: `skill-advisor-hook.md` and the docs that describe the Vibe and doctor code\n- Reason: the doctor code and its tests are confirmed; the hook contract's alias and Vibe claims\n  are the last surfaces to check against code\n- Rotation status: correctness, security, traceability and maintainability all exercised;\n  traceability and maintainability close in the next iteration\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach\n- Required evidence: the alias table against `hook-flags.cjs`, the Vibe rows against the adapter,\n  and a holdout-name sweep of the docs\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002 - traceability and maintainability\\n\\nLineage: `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b`. Iteration 2 of 3. Mode: review.\\nExecutor: this session, `cli-opencode` model `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Second iteration of the confirming round for the `vibe-hooks-doctor` area. State read first:\\n  `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-strategy.md`,\\n  `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, and `review/review-scope-5b.txt` for the area mapping.\\n- `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory at this iteration.\\n- The operator focus's doctor item (\\\"the doctor hooks-file reading\\\") and its docs item (\\\"docs\\n  agree with code\\\") are addressed here. The five `accuracy-runner` checks stay out of scope by\\n  `review-scope-5b.txt` and are not graded.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:40-77,110-200,227-273,367-393`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:39-63,238-310`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs:60-90,119-160,203-209`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:104-115,228-236`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/vibe-command-documents.md:16-36,126-143`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:250,343` and `acceptance-criteria.md:62`\\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe -- <the doctor script and its two tests>`\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The doctor README's Vibe sentence is false after the selector fix** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235` -- The row says \\\"a value with a trailing comment or a single-quoted string reads `hook-missing`\\\". Since `tomlCommands` now parses a `match` value as a basic or a literal string with an optional trailing comment (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:235-245,268-269`), a `match` value written in either shape reads `ok vibe`. The same row at `README.markdown:112` describes the Vibe reading without the new selector rule, so an operator whose `pre_agent` entry carries any other selector sees `hook-missing` and no describing doc explains it.\\n   Case: a `.vibe/hooks.toml` turn-start block written `match = 'main'`, or `match = \\\"main\\\"  # main agent only`, reads `ok vibe` with exit 0, while `README.markdown:235` says that shape reads `hook-missing`.\\n   Finding class: documentation_contract\\n   Scope proof: the README is the describing doc for the in-scope script; no other file states this sentence, and the script's own comments state the opposite rule.\\n   Affected surface hints: the doctor scripts README rows 112 and 235, and the operator repair path for a `hook-missing vibe` line.\\n2. **The new \\\"names the main agent\\\" case duplicates the default case, so it cannot fail for a reason of its own** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249-255` -- `vibeBlock`'s third parameter defaults to `match = \\\"main\\\"` (`:54`), so the new case writes byte-identical TOML to the case at `:241-247` and asserts the same exit code and line. The explicit-selector branch is already exercised by the default, so the added case can only fail when the older case fails too.\\n   Case: change `vibeBlock`'s default to `match = \\\"agents_spawn\\\"` and the two cases fail together; the new test never distinguishes an explicit selector from the default one.\\n   Finding class: test_hygiene\\n   Scope proof: both cases and the helper are in the in-scope test file; the sibling cases at `:257-271` and `:273-303` cover the absent and non-`main` branches.\\n   Affected surface hints: the doctor wiring suite's case list and the \\\"names the main agent\\\" title.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- **`spec_code` (core): partial.** Phase `032` REQ-007's doctor item is \\\"`hook-wiring-check.cjs`\\n  prints `hook-missing vibe` for `match = \\\"agents_spawn\\\"`\\\". A fixture with that selector printed\\n  `hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml` and exit 1, and the repository's own file printed\\n  `ok vibe` and exit 0, so the requirement holds. The same row's doc item covers\\n  `skill-advisor-hook.md`, not the doctor README, so finding 1 is a describing-doc gap rather\\n  than a contradicted requirement.\\n- **`checklist_evidence` (core): partial.** Phase `032` AC-007 names the same cases and all of\\n  them pass at this commit, including the contract-test rename and the `agents_spawn` refusal.\\n  The packet's AC row still reads `Unmet`; that is the phase's own close-out state and is\\n  recorded under Edge Cases, not graded here.\\n- **`skill_agent` (overlay): notApplicable.** No agent definition changed in this area.\\n- **`agent_cross_runtime` (overlay): pass.** The check covers five runtime files and the fix\\n  touches only the Vibe row; the other four readings are unchanged (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:40-77`)\\n  and the repository run prints `ok` for all five.\\n- **`feature_catalog_code` (overlay): notApplicable here.** Feature-catalog text is the\\n  `docs-metadata` area by `review-scope-5b.txt`.\\n- **`playbook_capability` (overlay): pass.** `CL-010` claims the document line after the head and\\n  an empty child-session result; iteration 1's probe printed exactly those, and no playbook\\n  covers the doctor check.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The doctor script reads the same `.vibe/hooks.toml` the runtime loads: the repository file's\\n  turn-start block carries `match = \\\"main\\\"` and the check prints `ok vibe`, so the selector rule\\n  is exercised against the shipped wiring rather than a fixture alone.\\n- The contract test's renamed case walks `MIRROR_CHECKS = [...DSH_CHECKS, ...VIBE_CHECKS]` and\\n  asserts `node <script> --check` for each (`doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs:88,119-137,203-205`),\\n  so its new title names exactly what it proves.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Phase `032`'s `acceptance-criteria.md:62` (AC-007) still reads `Unmet` while every item it names\\n  passes at this commit. The confirm round is not the phase close-out, so this is recorded as\\n  bookkeeping for the coordinator and not raised as a finding.\\n- The doctor README also describes the `--json` form; the fixture runs used the line form. Both\\n  forms share `inspect`, so the selector rule is the same, and the JSON form was not separately\\n  exercised.\\n- `re:` selectors read `hook-missing` by design (plan D9, pinned by the case at\\n  `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:273-280`). Not re-reported.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The selector rule matches plan D9 exactly: absent → `ok vibe`; `main` as a basic or literal\\n  string, with or without a trailing comment → `ok vibe`; any other value → `hook-missing vibe`\\n  (four fixtures, plus the repository's own file).\\n- An unparsable `match` line becomes a selector naming no agent, so a line the reader cannot\\n  parse narrows the match instead of widening it (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:238-245,268-269`).\\n- The block filter still requires the block's `type` to be the runtime's event and its `command`\\n  to be a string, so a `match` line cannot lend an entry to another event\\n  (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:271-272`).\\n- `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` printed\\n  `tests 50`, `pass 50`, `fail 0`, exit 0.\\n- The renamed contract test is accurate: `routeGaps` iterates both runtime check lists and\\n  enforces `node` plus `--check`, which is what \\\"every DSH and Vibe check in its check-only form\\\"\\n  means (`doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs:88,119-137`).\\n- `hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .` still prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor`, `ok devin`,\\n  `ok vibe` and exits 0, so the fix did not break the shipped wiring.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A `re:` selector that includes `main` is falsely reported.** Not raised: plan D9 decides that\\n  any value other than absent or exactly `main` reads `hook-missing`, \\\"`re:` selectors\\n  included\\\", and the case at `:273-280` pins the decision. Re-reporting it would need a new\\n  input that D9 does not already answer.\\n- **The three added cases after T023 make the suite count wrong.** T023's evidence says 47 tests\\n  and the suite now prints 50; T023a added three `match` cases, so the count is consistent with\\n  the task record and no case is unaccounted for.\\n- **A trailing-comment `type` or `command` line is now accepted.** Still refused: the entry regex\\n  anchors on the closing quote with no comment (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:263`), and the README's\\n  sentence stays true for those two keys. Only `match` gained comment tolerance.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability and traceability\\n- Focus area: `skill-advisor-hook.md` and the docs that describe the Vibe and doctor code\\n- Reason: the doctor code and its tests are confirmed; the hook contract's alias and Vibe claims\\n  are the last surfaces to check against code\\n- Rotation status: correctness, security, traceability and maintainability all exercised;\\n  traceability and maintainability close in the next iteration\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach\\n- Required evidence: the alias table against `hook-flags.cjs`, the Vibe rows against the adapter,\\n  and a holdout-name sweep of the docs\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781557131,"end":1794781579343}}}}
