 the false sentence is directly observable. If a later doc adds the selector rule, only the first clause remains.\",\n    scopeProof: \"The README is the describing doc for the in-scope doctor script; the script comments at :232-234 and :377-378 state the selector rule the README omits.\",\n    affectedSurfaceHints: [\"doctor scripts README rows 112 and 235\", \"operator repair path for hook-missing vibe\"]\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"C5B-P2-002\",\n    severity: \"P2\",\n    title: \"The new names-the-main-agent case duplicates the default case, so it cannot fail for a reason of its own\",\n    file: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249\",\n    findingClass: \"test_hygiene\",\n    claim: \"vibeBlock defaults to match = \\\"main\\\", so the case at :249-255 writes byte-identical TOML to :241-247 and asserts the same exit code and line; it adds no distinct branch.\",\n    evidenceRefs: [\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:54\", \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:241-247\", \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249-255\", \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:257-271\"],\n    counterevidenceSought: \"Compared the two rendered blocks and the helper default; also checked whether the new case exercises a different quoting shape or an explicit-versus-default distinction (it does not).\",\n    alternativeExplanation: \"The case may be intended as documentation of the explicit selector; as written it cannot distinguish an explicit selector from the default one.\",\n    finalSeverity: \"P2\",\n    confidence: \"high\",\n    downgradeTrigger: \"None; the duplicate is a direct read. If the helper default changes, the two cases diverge and the finding lapses.\",\n    scopeProof: \"Both cases and the helper are in the in-scope test file; the absent and non-main branches are already covered by :257-271 and :273-303.\",\n    affectedSurfaceHints: [\"doctor wiring suite case list\"]\n  }\n];\nconst record = {\n  type: \"iteration\",\n  iteration: 2,\n  mode: \"review\",\n  target_agent: \"deep-review\",\n  agent_definition_loaded: true,\n  resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\",\n  run: \"fanout-vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b-1794780590351-ezt1v0\",\n  status: \"complete\",\n  focus: \"traceability and maintainability\",\n  dimensions: [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n  filesReviewed: [\n    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:40-77,110-200,227-273,367-393\",\n    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:39-63,238-310\",\n    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs:60-90,119-160,203-209\",\n    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:104-115,228-236\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/vibe-command-documents.md:16-36,126-143\"\n  ],\n  findingsCount: 2,\n  findingsSummary: { P0: 0, P1: 0, P2: 2 },\n  findingsNew: [\"C5B-P2-001\", \"C5B-P2-002\"],\n  findingDetails: findings.map((f) => ({ id: f.id, severity: f.severity, title: f.title, file: f.file, findingClass: f.findingClass })),\n  traceabilityChecks: {\n    spec_code: { level: \"core\", status: \"partial\", notes: \"REQ-007's doctor item holds by fixture and by the repository run; its doc item covers the hook contract, not the doctor README, so C5B-P2-001 is a describing-doc gap.\" },\n    checklist_evidence: { level: \"core\", status: \"partial\", notes: \"AC-007's named cases all pass at this commit; the packet row still reads Unmet, which is the phase close-out state, recorded as an edge case.\" },\n    skill_agent: { level: \"overlay\", status: \"notApplicable\", notes: \"No agent definition changed in this area.\" },\n    agent_cross_runtime: { level: \"overlay\", status: \"pass\", notes: \"The check's five runtime rows are unchanged apart