{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781793580,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1547c44001T3HjE1I6o9bi3O","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e1544a43001iy5sCJwOaLI7yx","type":"tool","id":"call_51a0ff892d3c4efe8e482936","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003 - maintainability and traceability close-out\n\nLineage: `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b`. Iteration 3 of 3. Mode: review.\nExecutor: this session, `cli-opencode` model `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Third and final planned iteration of the confirming round. State read first:\n  `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-strategy.md`,\n  `deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\n- `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory at this iteration.\n- This iteration addresses the operator focus's two remaining clauses: the kill-switch names\n  agreeing between code and docs, and docs agreeing with code across the surfaces that describe\n  this area. The `accuracy-runner` focus checks remain out of scope by `review-scope-5b.txt`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:1-206`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78,234-285`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:44-96`\n- `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/README.md:1-33`\n- `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md:1-61`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/vibe-command-documents.md:1-151`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:104-115,228-236` (confirmation of iteration 2)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- **The kill-switch names agree in code and docs.** The doc's configuration table has ten\n  `NAME=1` rows. The resolver's own name set is `MASTER_FLAG`, `MASTER_ALIASES`,\n  `concernFlag('skill-advisor')` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']`, also ten names. A\n  comparison printed `missing from doc: none` and `extra in doc: none`, with both sets listed:\n  `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`,\n  `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`,\n  `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`,\n  `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`,\n  `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` (`hook-flags.cjs:38-78`).\n- **Every alias silences every adapter, as the doc now says.** All seven adapters reach the one\n  compiled Claude handler (`runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`) or the shared\n  resolver directly: the shims spawn that handler, Pi imports it, DSH and Vibe proxy it, and the\n  OpenCode plugin asks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')`\n  (`prompt-advisor.mjs:222`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:206`); the handler asks\n  the same resolver (`user-prompt-submit.ts:82-93`). So the `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`\n  row's \"Disables every adapter\" is true rather than the older native-only reading.\n- **The direct call's stated precedence holds.** `advisorDisabledBy` calls\n  `hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor', env, fileConfig)` with the caller's environment and the\n  flags file, and the resolver returns the environment value whenever the key is set\n  (`advisor-disabled.ts:84-95`, `hook-flags.cjs:243-246`), which is the doc's \"caller's\n  environment over `hook-flags.env`\".\n- **The standalone Python claim holds.** `skill_advisor.py` takes its disable name from\n  `COMPAT_CONTRACT[\"disabledEnv\"]`, which is `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`\n  (`runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json:3`), and refuses only on exactly `\"1\"`\n  (`skill_advisor.py:210,5491`). The doc's \"reads only this name, set to exactly `1`\" is accurate.\n- **The Vibe rows agree with the adapter.** The per-runtime row's `pre_agent`, `match` `main`,\n  runtime label `vibe`, child/subagent silence, head and directive repetition, and the one\n  document line per offered command all match `prompt-advisor.mjs:62-66,123-153,168-188,209-242`.\n  The start table's Vibe row (\"no command loader, the brief names the document\") matches the\n  same code.\n- **`skill_agent` (overlay): notApplicable.** No agent definition is in this area.\n- **`feature_catalog_code` (overlay): notApplicable here.** The feature catalog is the\n  `docs-metadata` area by `review-scope-5b.txt`; its own lineage verifies it.\n- **`playbook_capability` (overlay): pass.** `CL-010` names `withCommandDocuments`,\n  `buildAdvisorPart`, the document-line text and the child-session empty result, and every one of\n  those is what iteration 1's probe printed.\n- **Holdout hygiene.** A name search over `skill-advisor-hook.md`, the doctor README and `CL-010`\n  printed no corpus filename. No prompt file was opened at any iteration.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The hook contract's directory tree names `hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` as \"the real Vibe\n  part (the turn-start composer calls it)\" (`skill-advisor-hook.md:132-133`), and\n  `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/README.md:25` names the same file through the\n  `pre_agent` composer, so the two describing surfaces agree with each other and with the\n  adapter's import of the compiled handler.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Iteration 2's recorded `timestamp` was written from an estimate and reads ahead of the\n  gateway's `committed_at` for that record. The timestamp and duration are metadata; the\n  reducer orders iterations by the `iteration` number, and the finding counts, ids and prose all\n  agree between the narrative, the delta and the state log. Recorded here so the skew is not\n  mistaken for a reordering.\n- The doc's `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` row says the Python CLI reads \"only this name\";\n  the shared resolver also honours it, so the sentence is about the Python CLI's narrower rule,\n  not a claim that the name is Python-only. Read as written, it is accurate.\n- The two Vibe READMEs describe the receipt behavior and the child-session rule but not the\n  document line; `skill-advisor-hook.md` and `CL-010` carry that. No contradiction.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The doc's description line, per-runtime intro and start table all include Vibe after the fix\n  (`skill-advisor-hook.md:3,84,112`).\n- The four `MK_` rows and `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` describe the older aliases exactly as the resolver\n  reads them (`hook-flags.cjs:41,70-78`).\n- `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` no longer claims a native-only scope; the row, and the\n  paragraph after the table, say every adapter and the direct call (`skill-advisor-hook.md:174,184`).\n- The doctor README's `type`/`command` sentence remains true; only the `match` clause is the\n  iteration 2 finding (`README.markdown:235`).\n- `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/README.md:25` and\n  `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md` describe the same head-receipt behavior the\n  probe exercised in iteration 1.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The `MK_` rows are stale after the env-aliases bridge.** Ruled out: `env-aliases.cjs` maps\n  the older names onto the new ones and the resolver also lists them directly, so either path\n  silences the concern; the doc's \"older alias\" wording is accurate (iteration 3).\n- **The Codex, Cursor and Devin rows name a per-runtime advisor build that does not exist.**\n  Ruled out: the arrow's right side is the compiled shim under\n  `system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/<runtime>/`, which exists for all three, and the shim then\n  spawns the one advisor handler; the row describes that two-step dispatch (iteration 3).\n- **The Python CLI also reads the newer names.** Ruled out: it reads only\n  `COMPAT_CONTRACT[\"disabledEnv\"]` and compares to `\"1\"`; the newer names reach it only through\n  the env-alias bridge in the hook process, which the doc does not claim (iteration 3).\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining\n- Focus area: synthesis - the lineage report, the release-readiness state and the convergence record\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, no finding is active, and the three-iteration cap is reached\n- Rotation status: correctness, security, traceability and maintainability complete\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach; two P2 advisories are the remaining work\n- Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the three iteration final lines, the synthesis\n  close-out record and the report\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003 - maintainability and traceability close-out\\n\\nLineage: `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b`. Iteration 3 of 3. Mode: review.\\nExecutor: this session, `cli-opencode` model `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Third and final planned iteration of the confirming round. State read first:\\n  `deep-review-config.json`, `deep-review-state.jsonl`, `deep-review-strategy.md`,\\n  `deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\\n- `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage directory at this iteration.\\n- This iteration addresses the operator focus's two remaining clauses: the kill-switch names\\n  agreeing between code and docs, and docs agreeing with code across the surfaces that describe\\n  this area. The `accuracy-runner` focus checks remain out of scope by `review-scope-5b.txt`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:1-206`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-78,234-285`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:44-96`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/README.md:1-33`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md:1-61`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/vibe-command-documents.md:1-151`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:104-115,228-236` (confirmation of iteration 2)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- **The kill-switch names agree in code and docs.** The doc's configuration table has ten\\n  `NAME=1` rows. The resolver's own name set is `MASTER_FLAG`, `MASTER_ALIASES`,\\n  `concernFlag('skill-advisor')` and `LEGACY_ALIASES['skill-advisor']`, also ten names. A\\n  comparison printed `missing from doc: none` and `extra in doc: none`, with both sets listed:\\n  `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`,\\n  `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`,\\n  `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`,\\n  `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`,\\n  `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` (`hook-flags.cjs:38-78`).\\n- **Every alias silences every adapter, as the doc now says.** All seven adapters reach the one\\n  compiled Claude handler (`runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`) or the shared\\n  resolver directly: the shims spawn that handler, Pi imports it, DSH and Vibe proxy it, and the\\n  OpenCode plugin asks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')`\\n  (`prompt-advisor.mjs:222`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:206`); the handler asks\\n  the same resolver (`user-prompt-submit.ts:82-93`). So the `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`\\n  row's \\\"Disables every adapter\\\" is true rather than the older native-only reading.\\n- **The direct call's stated precedence holds.** `advisorDisabledBy` calls\\n  `hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor', env, fileConfig)` with the caller's environment and the\\n  flags file, and the resolver returns the environment value whenever the key is set\\n  (`advisor-disabled.ts:84-95`, `hook-flags.cjs:243-246`), which is the doc's \\\"caller's\\n  environment over `hook-flags.env`\\\".\\n- **The standalone Python claim holds.** `skill_advisor.py` takes its disable name from\\n  `COMPAT_CONTRACT[\\\"disabledEnv\\\"]`, which is `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`\\n  (`runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json:3`), and refuses only on exactly `\\\"1\\\"`\\n  (`skill_advisor.py:210,5491`). The doc's \\\"reads only this name, set to exactly `1`\\\" is accurate.\\n- **The Vibe rows agree with the adapter.** The per-runtime row's `pre_agent`, `match` `main`,\\n  runtime label `vibe`, child/subagent silence, head and directive repetition, and the one\\n  document line per offered command all match `prompt-advisor.mjs:62-66,123-153,168-188,209-242`.\\n  The start table's Vibe row (\\\"no command loader, the brief names the document\\\") matches the\\n  same code.\\n- **`skill_agent` (overlay): notApplicable.** No agent definition is in this area.\\n- **`feature_catalog_code` (overlay): notApplicable here.** The feature catalog is the\\n  `docs-metadata` area by `review-scope-5b.txt`; its own lineage verifies it.\\n- **`playbook_capability` (overlay): pass.** `CL-010` names `withCommandDocuments`,\\n  `buildAdvisorPart`, the document-line text and the child-session empty result, and every one of\\n  those is what iteration 1's probe printed.\\n- **Holdout hygiene.** A name search over `skill-advisor-hook.md`, the doctor README and `CL-010`\\n  printed no corpus filename. No prompt file was opened at any iteration.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The hook contract's directory tree names `hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs` as \\\"the real Vibe\\n  part (the turn-start composer calls it)\\\" (`skill-advisor-hook.md:132-133`), and\\n  `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/README.md:25` names the same file through the\\n  `pre_agent` composer, so the two describing surfaces agree with each other and with the\\n  adapter's import of the compiled handler.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Iteration 2's recorded `timestamp` was written from an estimate and reads ahead of the\\n  gateway's `committed_at` for that record. The timestamp and duration are metadata; the\\n  reducer orders iterations by the `iteration` number, and the finding counts, ids and prose all\\n  agree between the narrative, the delta and the state log. Recorded here so the skew is not\\n  mistaken for a reordering.\\n- The doc's `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` row says the Python CLI reads \\\"only this name\\\";\\n  the shared resolver also honours it, so the sentence is about the Python CLI's narrower rule,\\n  not a claim that the name is Python-only. Read as written, it is accurate.\\n- The two Vibe READMEs describe the receipt behavior and the child-session rule but not the\\n  document line; `skill-advisor-hook.md` and `CL-010` carry that. No contradiction.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The doc's description line, per-runtime intro and start table all include Vibe after the fix\\n  (`skill-advisor-hook.md:3,84,112`).\\n- The four `MK_` rows and `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` describe the older aliases exactly as the resolver\\n  reads them (`hook-flags.cjs:41,70-78`).\\n- `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED` no longer claims a native-only scope; the row, and the\\n  paragraph after the table, say every adapter and the direct call (`skill-advisor-hook.md:174,184`).\\n- The doctor README's `type`/`command` sentence remains true; only the `match` clause is the\\n  iteration 2 finding (`README.markdown:235`).\\n- `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/vibe/README.md:25` and\\n  `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/README.md` describe the same head-receipt behavior the\\n  probe exercised in iteration 1.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The `MK_` rows are stale after the env-aliases bridge.** Ruled out: `env-aliases.cjs` maps\\n  the older names onto the new ones and the resolver also lists them directly, so either path\\n  silences the concern; the doc's \\\"older alias\\\" wording is accurate (iteration 3).\\n- **The Codex, Cursor and Devin rows name a per-runtime advisor build that does not exist.**\\n  Ruled out: the arrow's right side is the compiled shim under\\n  `system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/<runtime>/`, which exists for all three, and the shim then\\n  spawns the one advisor handler; the row describes that two-step dispatch (iteration 3).\\n- **The Python CLI also reads the newer names.** Ruled out: it reads only\\n  `COMPAT_CONTRACT[\\\"disabledEnv\\\"]` and compares to `\\\"1\\\"`; the newer names reach it only through\\n  the env-alias bridge in the hook process, which the doc does not claim (iteration 3).\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining\\n- Focus area: synthesis - the lineage report, the release-readiness state and the convergence record\\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered, no finding is active, and the three-iteration cap is reached\\n- Rotation status: correctness, security, traceability and maintainability complete\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approach; two P2 advisories are the remaining work\\n- Required evidence: the registry's active counts, the three iteration final lines, the synthesis\\n  close-out record and the report\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confir