{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781933742,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1568456001O08qflOWjyyuqF","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75cbffeKCKhhfHEFy30Ji","messageID":"msg_1e15673fa001ZAcJ1yIdhB5R5P","type":"tool","id":"call_007954ceccac4db88f8d322e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - pass five confirming round 5b, vibe-hooks-doctor area\n\nLineage: `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b`. Review target:\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`. Mode: review.\nIterations: 3 of 3. Session: `fanout-vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b-1794780590351-ezt1v0`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict: PASS**\n- **hasAdvisories: true** (two active P2 items)\n- **Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=2**\n- **Review scope**: the eight `vibe-hooks-doctor` files from `review/review-scope-5b.txt` for the\n  commit range `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe`, plus the docs that describe them\n  (`doctor/scripts/README.markdown`, `skill-advisor-hook.md`, the Vibe hook READMEs and `CL-010`).\n- **Operator review focus**: Confirming round 5b of code review pass five of command surfacing.\n  Read `review/review-brief-5b.txt` in the packet first and follow it. Review the files in\n  `review/review-scope-5b.txt` whose area equals your lineage label without its `-confirm-5b`\n  suffix, plus docs that describe them. Each finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a\n  concrete input. Check that the shell write reader misses no in-place edit, the COMMAND reader\n  reads only a line the model printed as its own, the arena builder refuses a dirty source, a\n  stale build, an escaping or absolute link and answers a failed check with a JSON line, a live\n  turn checks for a remote every turn and has no network push, the kill-switch names agree in\n  code and docs, and docs agree with code. Never open command-prompts.jsonl,\n  holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq del(.prompt). Change\n  no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\n\nThe pass-five fixes in this area hold. The hook sources now read the fallback context unchanged,\nfollow the injected environment for the head receipt, and find the kill-switch resolver from both\nthe source and the built folder; the doctor now reads the Vibe `match` selector and refuses a\nnon-`main` entry; the contract test's new name matches what it asserts; the hook contract names\nVibe in its three places and states the alias scope the resolver implements. Two P2 advisories\nremain: the doctor scripts README still contains a sentence the selector fix made false, and the\nnew \"names the main agent\" case duplicates the default case instead of covering a new branch.\n\nFive of the operator focus's seven checks belong to the `accuracy-runner` area by\n`review-scope-5b.txt` and were not graded here.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this lineage. The verdict is PASS with advisories; the\ntwo P2 items are documentation and test-hygiene work that can be folded into the remediation\nphase's close-out or a later docs pass. The block below still carries them so a plan run can pick\nthem up without re-reading the prose.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C5B-P2-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The doctor README still says a single-quoted or trailing-comment value reads hook-missing, and never names the match selector rule\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"documentation_contract\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C5B-P2-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"The new names-the-main-agent case duplicates the default case, so it cannot fail for a reason of its own\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"test_hygiene\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    \"Advisory A: correct README.markdown row 235 and name the selector rule in row 112.\",\n    \"Advisory B: drop the duplicate case or give it a shape the helper default does not write.\"\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": \"No new spec. Record the two advisories in the remediation packet's close-out.\",\n  \"planSeed\": \"No new plan. If picked up, one docs edit and one test edit.\",\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"documentation_contract\", \"test_hygiene\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"doctor scripts README rows 112 and 235\",\n    \"doctor wiring suite case list\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Title | Dimension | File:line | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| C5B-P2-001 | P2 | Doctor README sentence made false by the selector fix; selector rule undocumented | traceability | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235` | active |\n| C5B-P2-002 | P2 | New \"names the main agent\" case duplicates the default case | maintainability | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249` | active |\n\n### C5B-P2-001\n\n- **Evidence**: the row says \"a value with a trailing comment or a single-quoted string reads\n  `hook-missing`\"; four fixtures and the repository run show `match = 'main'` and\n  `match = \"main\"  # main agent only` print `ok vibe` with exit 0, while `match = \"agents_spawn\"`\n  prints `hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml` with exit 1.\n- **Impact**: an operator whose `pre_agent` entry carries any other selector sees `hook-missing`\n  and no describing doc explains the rule; the same row is the only account of the Vibe reading.\n- **Fix recommendation**: scope the trailing-comment/single-quote clause to `type` and `command`,\n  and state the selector rule (absent or exactly `main` reads wired).\n- **findingClass**: documentation_contract\n- **scopeProof**: the README is the describing doc for the in-scope script; the script comments at\n  `:232-234` and `:377-378` state the rule the README omits.\n- **affectedSurfaceHints**: doctor scripts README rows 112 and 235; operator repair path for a\n  `hook-missing vibe` line.\n\n### C5B-P2-002\n\n- **Evidence**: `vibeBlock`'s third parameter defaults to `match = \"main\"` (`:54`), so `:249-255`\n  writes byte-identical TOML to `:241-247` and asserts the same two outcomes.\n- **Impact**: the case list suggests an explicit-selector branch that no distinct input reaches;\n  it can only fail when the older case already fails.\n- **Fix recommendation**: drop the case, or give it a shape the default does not write (a selector\n  on a second block, or `match` before `type`).\n- **findingClass**: test_hygiene\n- **scopeProof**: both cases and the helper are in the in-scope test file; the absent and\n  non-`main` branches are covered at `:257-271` and `:273-303`.\n- **affectedSurfaceHints**: doctor wiring suite case list.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n### P0\n\nNone.\n\n### P1\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 advisories (not blocking)\n\n1. **Docs**: edit `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown` rows 112 and 235 as above.\n2. **Tests**: replace or remove the duplicate case at `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249-255`.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- No spec change is required. If the two advisories are recorded, add one line to the\n  remediation packet's close-out: the doctor README and its test list are the only surfaces the\n  confirming round left open.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Task A: rewrite `doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235` to say the trailing-comment and\n  single-quote limits apply to `type` and `command`, and that a `match` selector reads wired only\n  when it is absent or `main`; mention the selector beside the Vibe reading at `:112`.\n- Task B: delete `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249-255`, or point it at a distinct TOML shape and\n  assert the same `ok vibe` line.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | pass | Phase `032` REQ-007's items hold: directive-only context unchanged, receipt follows the injected env, the Claude hook from source honors `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `agents_spawn` reads `hook-missing vibe`, the contract test carries its new name, and the hook contract names Vibe in three places. The doctor README gap is a describing-doc issue, not a contradicted requirement. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | Every case phase `032` AC-007 names passes at this commit. The packet's AC row still reads `Unmet` until the phase closes; recorded as bookkeeping, not graded. |\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | All seven adapters reach the one compiled handler or the shared resolver; the doctor reads five runtime files and prints `ok` for all five in this checkout. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | The feature catalog is the `docs-metadata` area by `review-scope-5b.txt`. |\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | `CL-010`'s document-line and child-session claims match the iteration 1 probe. |\n\n### AC_COVERAGE\n\n`exempt`: the review target is the phase-parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`, which has no\n`checklist.md` or `acceptance-criteria.md` at its root; the acceptance criteria live in the child\nphase `032-review-pass-five-remediation`.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- The `accuracy-runner` focus checks (in-place shell writes, the COMMAND line reader, arena\n  provenance, the live-turn remote guard) are deferred to their own lineage by\n  `review-scope-5b.txt`.\n- Rebuild freshness of the untracked `runtime/dist` copy is the build contract, not a review item.\n- `R1-P2-002` (Vibe `parent_session_id`) stays rejected per `review/verify-5/report.md` and plan\n  D13; `re:` selectors in the doctor stay `hook-missing` per plan D9.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated directions: none\n- Selected review directions: correctness and security (iteration 1), traceability and\n  maintainability (iterations 2 and 3)\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence Summary\n\n- Iterations run: 3 of 3 (`maxIterationsReached`).\n- New-findings ratio per iteration: 0.00, 1.00, 0.00.\n- Active findings after the final reduction: P0=0, P1=0, P2=2.\n- Every iteration's final line is `Review verdict: PASS`.\n\n### Coverage Summary\n\n| Dimension | Iterations | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| correctness | 1 | covered |\n| security | 1 | covered |\n| traceability | 2, 3 | covered |\n| maintainability | 2, 3 | covered |\n\n### Ruled-Out Claims\n\n- The unbounded ancestor walk loads a foreign resolver: frozen by plan D9, identical sibling in\n  `advisor-disabled.ts:50-68`.\n- The directive-only early return skips a real head: only the no-brief fallback opens that way.\n- A missing resolver now fails closed: null answers enabled.\n- A `re:` selector that includes `main` is falsely reported: frozen by plan D9 and pinned by test.\n- A trailing-comment `type`/`command` line is now accepted: the entry regex still refuses it.\n- The Codex/Cursor/Devin rows name a per-runtime advisor build: they name the compiled shim.\n- The Python CLI also reads the newer switch names: it reads only `disabledEnv`, exactly `\"1\"`.\n- The `MK_` rows are stale after the env-aliases bridge: the bridge and the alias list both honour\n  them.\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n- The eight scoped files and the docs that describe them, listed in\n  `deep-review-config.json` and in each iteration's `Files Reviewed`.\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe -- <scoped paths>`.\n- `review/review-brief-5b.txt`, `review/review-focus-5b.txt`, `review/review-scope-5b.txt`,\n  `review/verify-5/report.md`, plan D9/D13 and the two scratch reports.\n\n### Cross-Reference Appendix\n\nCore: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` partial (packet close-out pending). Overlay:\n`agent_cross_runtime` and `playbook_capability` pass; `skill_agent` and `feature_catalog_code`\nnot applicable to this area.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report - pass five confirming round 5b, vibe-hooks-doctor area\\n\\nLineage: `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b`. Review target:\\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`. Mode: review.\\nIterations: 3 of 3. Session: `fanout-vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b-1794780590351-ezt1v0`.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict: PASS**\\n- **hasAdvisories: true** (two active P2 items)\\n- **Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=2**\\n- **Review scope**: the eight `vibe-hooks-doctor` files from `review/review-scope-5b.txt` for the\\n  commit range `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe`, plus the docs that describe them\\n  (`doctor/scripts/README.markdown`, `skill-advisor-hook.md`, the Vibe hook READMEs and `CL-010`).\\n- **Operator review focus**: Confirming round 5b of code review pass five of command surfacing.\\n  Read `review/review-brief-5b.txt` in the packet first and follow it. Review the files in\\n  `review/review-scope-5b.txt` whose area equals your lineage label without its `-confirm-5b`\\n  suffix, plus docs that describe them. Each finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a\\n  concrete input. Check that the shell write reader misses no in-place edit, the COMMAND reader\\n  reads only a line the model printed as its own, the arena builder refuses a dirty source, a\\n  stale build, an escaping or absolute link and answers a failed check with a JSON line, a live\\n  turn checks for a remote every turn and has no network push, the kill-switch names agree in\\n  code and docs, and docs agree with code. Never open command-prompts.jsonl,\\n  holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq del(.prompt). Change\\n  no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\\n\\nThe pass-five fixes in this area hold. The hook sources now read the fallback context unchanged,\\nfollow the injected environment for the head receipt, and find the kill-switch resolver from both\\nthe source and the built folder; the doctor now reads the Vibe `match` selector and refuses a\\nnon-`main` entry; the contract test's new name matches what it asserts; the hook contract names\\nVibe in its three places and states the alias scope the resolver implements. Two P2 advisories\\nremain: the doctor scripts README still contains a sentence the selector fix made false, and the\\nnew \\\"names the main agent\\\" case duplicates the default case instead of covering a new branch.\\n\\nFive of the operator focus's seven checks belong to the `accuracy-runner` area by\\n`review-scope-5b.txt` and were not graded here.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this lineage. The verdict is PASS with advisories; the\\ntwo P2 items are documentation and test-hygiene work that can be folded into the remediation\\nphase's close-out or a later docs pass. The block below still carries them so a plan run can pick\\nthem up without re-reading the prose.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C5B-P2-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The doctor README still says a single-quoted or trailing-comment value reads hook-missing, and never names the match selector rule\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"documentation_contract\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"C5B-P2-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The new names-the-main-agent case duplicates the default case, so it cannot fail for a reason of its own\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"test_hygiene\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    \\\"Advisory A: correct README.markdown row 235 and name the selector rule in row 112.\\\",\\n    \\\"Advisory B: drop the duplicate case or give it a shape the helper default does not write.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": \\\"No new spec. Record the two advisories in the remediation packet's close-out.\\\",\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": \\\"No new plan. If picked up, one docs edit and one test edit.\\\",\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"documentation_contract\\\", \\\"test_hygiene\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"doctor scripts README rows 112 and 235\\\",\\n    \\\"doctor wiring suite case list\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Title | Dimension | File:line | Disposition |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| C5B-P2-001 | P2 | Doctor README sentence made false by the selector fix; selector rule undocumented | traceability | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235` | active |\\n| C5B-P2-002 | P2 | New \\\"names the main agent\\\" case duplicates the default case | maintainability | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249` | active |\\n\\n### C5B-P2-001\\n\\n- **Evidence**: the row says \\\"a value with a trailing comment or a single-quoted string reads\\n  `hook-missing`\\\"; four fixtures and the repository run show `match = 'main'` and\\n  `match = \\\"main\\\"  # main agent only` print `ok vibe` with exit 0, while `match = \\\"agents_spawn\\\"`\\n  prints `hook-missing vibe .vibe/hooks.toml` with exit 1.\\n- **Impact**: an operator whose `pre_agent` entry carries any other selector sees `hook-missing`\\n  and no describing doc explains the rule; the same row is the only account of the Vibe reading.\\n- **Fix recommendation**: scope the trailing-comment/single-quote clause to `type` and `command`,\\n  and state the selector rule (absent or exactly `main` reads wired).\\n- **findingClass**: documentation_contract\\n- **scopeProof**: the README is the describing doc for the in-scope script; the script comments at\\n  `:232-234` and `:377-378` state the rule the README omits.\\n- **affectedSurfaceHints**: doctor scripts README rows 112 and 235; operator repair path for a\\n  `hook-missing vibe` line.\\n\\n### C5B-P2-002\\n\\n- **Evidence**: `vibeBlock`'s third parameter defaults to `match = \\\"main\\\"` (`:54`), so `:249-255`\\n  writes byte-identical TOML to `:241-247` and asserts the same two outcomes.\\n- **Impact**: the case list suggests an explicit-selector branch that no distinct input reaches;\\n  it can only fail when the older case already fails.\\n- **Fix recommendation**: drop the case, or give it a shape the default does not write (a selector\\n  on a second block, or `match` before `type`).\\n- **findingClass**: test_hygiene\\n- **scopeProof**: both cases and the helper are in the in-scope test file; the absent and\\n  non-`main` branches are covered at `:257-271` and `:273-303`.\\n- **affectedSurfaceHints**: doctor wiring suite case list.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n### P0\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 advisories (not blocking)\\n\\n1. **Docs**: edit `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown` rows 112 and 235 as above.\\n2. **Tests**: replace or remove the duplicate case at `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249-255`.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- No spec change is required. If the two advisories are recorded, add one line to the\\n  remediation packet's close-out: the doctor README and its test list are the only surfaces the\\n  confirming round left open.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Task A: rewrite `doctor/scripts/README.markdown:235` to say the trailing-comment and\\n  single-quote limits apply to `type` and `command`, and that a `match` selector reads wired only\\n  when it is absent or `main`; mention the selector beside the Vibe reading at `:112`.\\n- Task B: delete `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:249-255`, or point it at a distinct TOML shape and\\n  assert the same `ok vibe` line.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | Phase `032` REQ-007's items hold: directive-only context unchanged, receipt follows the injected env, the Claude hook from source honors `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `agents_spawn` reads `hook-missing vibe`, the contract test carries its new name, and the hook contract names Vibe in three places. The doctor README gap is a describing-doc issue, not a contradicted requirement. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | Every case phase `032` AC-007 names passes at this commit. The packet's AC row still reads `Unmet` until the phase closes; recorded as bookkeeping, not graded. |\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass | All seven adapters reach the one compiled handler or the shared resolver; the doctor reads five runtime files and prints `ok` for all five in this checkout. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | The feature catalog is the `docs-metadata` area by `review-scope-5b.txt`. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | pass | `CL-010`'s document-line and child-session claims match the iteration 1 probe. |\\n\\n### AC_COVERAGE\\n\\n`exempt`: the review target is the phase-parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`, which has no\\n`checklist.md` or `acceptance-criteria.md` at its root; the acceptance criteria live in the child\\nphase `032-review-pass-five-remediation`.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- The `accuracy-runner` focus checks (in-place shell writes, the COMMAND line reader, arena\\n  provenance, the live-turn remote guard) are deferred to their own lineage by\\n  `review-scope-5b.txt`.\\n- Rebuild freshness of the untracked `runtime/dist` copy is the build contract, not a review item.\\n- `R1-P2-002` (Vibe `parent_session_id`) stays rejected per `review/verify-5/report.md` and plan\\n  D13; `re:` selectors in the doctor stay `hook-missing` per plan D9.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated directions: none\\n- Selected review directions: correctness and security (iteration 1), traceability and\\n  maintainability (iterations 2 and 3)\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence Summary\\n\\n- Iterations run: 3 of 3 (`maxIterationsReached`).\\n- New-findings ratio per iteration: 0.00, 1.00, 0.00.\\n- Active findings after the final reduction: P0=0, P1=0, P2=2.\\n- Every iteration's final line is `Review verdict: PASS`.\\n\\n### Coverage Summary\\n\\n| Dimension | Iterations | Status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| correctness | 1 | covered |\\n| security | 1 | covered |\\n| traceability | 2, 3 | covered |\\n| maintainability | 2, 3 | covered |\\n\\n### Ruled-Out Claims\\n\\n- The unbounded ancestor walk loads a foreign resolver: frozen by plan D9, identical sibling in\\n  `advisor-disabled.ts:50-68`.\\n- The directive-only early return skips a real head: only the no-brief fallback opens that way.\\n- A missing resolver now fails closed: null answers enabled.\\n- A `re:` selector that includes `main` is falsely reported: frozen by plan D9 and pinned by test.\\n- A trailing-comment `type`/`command` line is now accepted: the entry regex still refuses it.\\n- The Codex/Cursor/Devin rows name a per-runtime advisor build: they name the compiled shim.\\n- The Python CLI also reads the newer switch names: it reads only `disabledEnv`, exactly `\\\"1\\\"`.\\n- The `MK_` rows are stale after the env-aliases bridge: the bridge and the alias list both honour\\n  them.\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n- The eight scoped files and the docs that describe them, listed in\\n  `deep-review-config.json` and in each iteration's `Files Reviewed`.\\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2a1a42263cc d21dbc1cafe -- <scoped paths>`.\\n- `review/review-brief-5b.txt`, `review/review-focus-5b.txt`, `review/review-scope-5b.txt`,\\n  `review/verify-5/report.md`, plan D9/D13 and the two scratch reports.\\n\\n### Cross-Reference Appendix\\n\\nCore: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` partial (packet close-out pending). Overlay:\\n`agent_cross_runtime` and `playbook_capability` pass; `skill_agent` and `feature_catalog_code`\\nnot applicable to this area.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781906006,"end":1794781933742}}}}
